\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Midday Flat; Sentiment Boosted By Yen, HKMA Moves \b0\par\par\uc2 368 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 1998\par 06:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is stable in light dealings midday Wednesday, with market sentiment improved because of the strengthening yen and market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Around 0410 GMT (12:10 a.m. EDT), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7490 per U.S. dollar, slightly weaker than the opening of HK$7.7485 and unchanged from late Tuesday's levels. The dollar has moved between HK$7.7490 and HK$7.7493 so far Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Money market and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said that the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  was offering HK$200 million in the three-month money market, helping to boost liquidity. \par \par \uc2  Interbank rates and forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums also eased following HKMA's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday. But dealers said midday Wednesday there was no sign of HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in morning dealings. \par \par \uc2  Still, the Wednesday money market activity is keeping weakening pressure off of the spot exchange rate, a treasury head at a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  Moreover, the stronger yen helped ease fears of further immediate pressure on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. At 0439 GMT (12:39 a.m. EDT), the yen is trading at around Y146.19 to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 7.25%, down from 8.00% late Tuesday. The three-month rate is 11.5%, down from 12.25% previously. For more Hibor news, please refer to Telerate page [1085]. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong dollar forward premiums rose slightly, with one dealer saying cautious investors moved to hedge, after seeing some light overseas buying in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Typically, when speculators operate in the forward market, premiums rise more sharply because they're taking on much larger positions. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the forward \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, the six-month premium is\par quoted at 2,650 points, up from 2,500 late Tuesday, while the one-year\par premium was quoted at 5,150 points, down from 5,400 previously.\par    -By Belinda Rabano; (852) 2802 7002; brabano@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 12-08-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0455GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8c06toz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
