\par\par \b \uc2  Taiwan c.bank vows to maintain  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  stability. \b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 1998\par 06:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TAIPEI, Aug 9 (Reuters) - Taiwan's deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Shea Jia-dong has vowed to maintain the Taiwan dollar's stability, saying the island would not join a race of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation, local media reported on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will do its best to maintain stability of the Taiwan dollar and will not join a competition of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation," Taiwan newspapers quoted Shea as telling U.S. finance and Federal Reserve officials in Washington on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  "We know what role we should play," said Shea, who was in the United States to attend the vice-ministerial level trade talks between Washington and Taipei. \par \par \uc2  Washington has expressed concerns over the Taiwan dollar's movement, fearing a sharp fall would add further downward pressure to Asia's already-battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , local reports said. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar has fallen about 19 percent to the U.S. dollar since Asia's financial woes erupted in mid-1997, far below the depreciations of its regional export rivals. This is eroding Taiwan's export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  In July, Taiwan exports fell 16.3 percent in July from a year earlier period to US$8.955 billion, hammered by sharply lower demand from Japan and other recession-hit Asian trade partners. \par \par \uc2  Shea reportedly told U.S. officials that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would try to eliminate "unnecessary fluctuations" of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and maintain what he called a "dynamic stability" of the Taiwan dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly pledged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when "seasonal, occasional and abnormal" factors emerged. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar closed at a seven-week low of T$34.60 on Friday, with investors seeking a safe haven in the U.S. dollar amid renewed concerns about depreciation pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar and China's yuan. \par \par \uc2  Dealers noted the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's downturn but said the bank seemed prepared to tolerate wider fluctuations than it has in recent days. ((Taipei newsroom, +886 2 2508-0815 fax +886 2 2508-0204, taipei.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8902r1h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
