\par\par \b \uc2  Heavy HK dollar sales for third day. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Angi Li Yeung \par \uc2 768 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 1998\par 07:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Aug 7 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar came under renewed pressure on Friday as overseas investment houses kept up their assault on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  Since Wednesday, four U.S. investment banks as well as fund houses have been aggressively selling the Hong Kong dollar short, they said. Selling continued on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S.-based fund houses were aggressively buying forwards today. The size of the short sales was quite big," a dealer at a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  The heavy sales of Hong Kong dollars have raised fears about the resilience of the Hong Kong dollar's peg to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar is linked to the U.S. unit at a rate of HK$7.8 per US$1 and is permitted to float in a narrow band around that level. It was at HK$7.7490/00 per dollar at midday on Friday, a level viewed as key support. \par \par \uc2  The peg was instituted in 1983 during \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  instability that accompanied early negotiations between Britain and China on Hong Kong's future. Since then, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fluctuated narrowly. \par \par \uc2  But the local dollar has come under attack sporadically over the past year, a victim of Asia's financial crisis and Hong Kong's severe economic downturn. \par \par \uc2  The government on Monday said the economy contracted 2.8 percent in the first quarter of 1998, a bigger decline than the two percent forecast in May. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong authorities have said the economy will worsen before it gets better and economists predict a full-year recession. \par \par \uc2  The poor economic prognosis, coupled with weak interim results for Hong Kong companies, has cast a pall over sentiment in the territory and left the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  open to attack, analysts said. The market was particularly vulnerable after months of worry over the weak yen, they said. \par \par \uc2  A sagging Chinese yuan also has accentuated fears Beijing could devalue the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a move that many believe could imperil the Hong Kong dollar peg. \par \par \uc2  Several billions of U.S. dollars worth of Hong Kong dollars have been sold over the past few days in both the spot and forward markets, dealers and analysts said. \par \par \uc2  In Bangkok, Thailand's deputy prime minister, Supachai Panitchpakdi, said on Friday the speculative attacks against the Hong Kong dollar were undermining regional confidence. \par \par \uc2  "The problem in Hong Kong is now becoming a regional problem and Thailand is concerned about it because it could affect our efforts to solve the problems that we have here," he told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Because the Hong Kong dollar is pegged, assaults on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually are made in the forward market, where there is more room for fluctuations. Selling spot Hong Kong dollars implies fears the peg could snap soon, some analysts said. \par \par \uc2  By midday on Friday, the three-month forward spread had climbed to 1,400-1,500 points, well above the 650-700 points registered on Tuesday, the day before the attack began. \par \par \uc2  Interest rates were sharply higher. The benchmark three-month Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate was at an eight week high of 12.69 percent at Friday's 0330 GMT fixing compared with 11.14 percent at the same time on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The one-month rate was even higher at 13.2 percent versus 11.06 percent on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The intense pressure on the Hong Kong dollar has caused jitters throughout Asia. While up to now, weakness in the yen and the yuan have hurt the Hong Kong unit, the salvos against the Hong Kong dollar are now harming those \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong dealers said the scale of the attack over the past three days was comparable to that of October 1997, when the overnight rate ballooned to 300 percent as the territory came under the most severe speculative attack since 1983. \par \par \uc2  "Though turning a bit bearish, the market has remained calm and it is not as panicky as it was last October," said Andy Lim, head of money market and interest rate trading at NatWest Markets in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  "Perhaps we have all well-prepared for it. The market, the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Hong Kong citizen are better-equipped after repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  attacks over the past year," he said. \par \par \uc2  The HKMA has said it has recently borrowed and bought Hong Kong dollars to fund a shortfall in the government treasury, but said the purchases did not represent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  Newsroom (852) 2843-6371; Fax (852) 2845-0636 \par \par \uc2  - Email: hongkong.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du87028x9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
