\par\par \b \uc2  HK Stk Mkt/Anniversary -2: Scenario Worse Than Imagined \b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 1998\par 11:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Amid these mounting fears, local interbank interest rates climbed higher Friday and, though the Hong Kong dollar remained fairly steady, the week was marked by selling of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at levels dangerously close to the key level of HK$7.7500 to the U.S. dollar, at which point the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was quoted at HK$7.7495 Friday, little changed from HK$7.7501 quoted in London overnight. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong interbank offered rate was quoted late Friday at 7.5%, up from 5.5% late Thursday. The benchmark three-month rate was at 12.75%, up from 10.75% the previous day. \par \par \uc2  Despite the steeper rates, the Hong Kong Association of Banks didn't raise interest rates at its weekly meeting Friday. \par \par \uc2  In the past year, "the whole macro scenario has worsened and it's so much worse than anyone could have guessed," said Gilbert Wong, managing director at BNP Prime Peregrine Securities (HK) Ltd. "And on top of that, the Asian crisis is still lingering on; there's been a steep downturn in the property market, and it's had a severe impact on banks." \par \par \uc2  Add to those woes, the recent "assault on the Hong Kong dollar and a lot of renminbi (yuan) black market activity," and it's no surprise the market is hovering near five-year lows, Wong said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 07-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0951GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8706q17\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picsc