\par\par \b \uc2  HK Late Hibor Up As  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Woes Cast Pall On Sentiment \b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 1998\par 11:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong interbank rates were higher late Friday as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jitters continued to maul sentiment and virtually close down the local money market. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong offered rate is quoted at 7.5%, up from 5.5% late Thursday. The three-month rate is 12.75%, up from 10.75% late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  However, in a moribund market, the rates don't mean much dealers said. "There isn't a market in the cash," said one local money market dealer. "It's theoretical." \par \par \uc2  Rates are higher after news that the Vietnamese dong has been devalued by about 10% in local terms. While it's not a freely-convertible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the devaluation didn't help sentiment, which is already pessimistic. \par \par \uc2  The yen's move back through 145.00 per U.S. dollar is also casting a pall over the market ahead of the weekend. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they're also keeping a watchful eye on the Hong Kong dollar, which is flirting with a key support level of HK$7.7500, seen as a trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums also remain high, and dealers said some smaller hedge funds are believed to be short-selling the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  In the futures market, the three-month September contract is quoted at 88.30 for an underlying money market rate of 11.70%. It has moved between 87.89 with a yield of 12.11% and 88.60 for a yield of 11.40% on turnover of 2,709 lots. \par \par \uc2  Late Friday, the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7500 per U.S. dollar, barely changed from HK$7.7501 recorded late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 07-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0921GMT \par \par \uc2  1085 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8706px6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
