\par\par \b \uc2  HK/Hibor/Opens -2: All Eyes On Spot HK Dlr, Forwards \b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 1998\par 04:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong interbank rates rose early Friday on fears that speculators aren't going to leave the territory anytime soon, particularly now that the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is flirting with a key support level. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rates is quoted at 7.25%, up from 5.5% late Thursday. The three-month rate is 11.5%, up from 10.75%. For more Hibor news, please refer to Telerate page [1085]. \par \par \uc2  Attention is focused on the spot Hong Kong dollar after its trading overnight in London above HK$7.7500, which is seen as a trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they haven't seen any deals completed in the three-month maturity, which is too rich at current levels for most borrowers' taste. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect activity to remain subdued until banks have a better idea of what's going to happen with the spot Hong Kong dollar and forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums. \par \par \uc2  Forwards are being pushed up in the six-month and one-year maturity due to speculative buying. \par \par \uc2  Early Friday, the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7500 per U.S. dollar, weaker than the HK$7.7498 recorded late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2802 7002; skennedy@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 07-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0213GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8706oy7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex