\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Opens -2: Most Banks Sidelined \b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 1998\par 03:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar was stronger early Friday after breaching a key support level overnight in offshore markets. \par \par \uc2  Around 0100 GMT (9 p.m. EDT Thursday), the Hong Kong dollar was quoted at HK$7.7490 per U.S. dollar, stronger than the HK$7.7501 quoted overnight in London. The Hong Kong dollar has traded in a range of HK$7.7493 and HK$7.7495 so far Friday. \par \par \uc2  Attention is focused on the spot Hong Kong dollar after its trading overnight in London above HK$7.7500, which is seen as a trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  An Australian bank dealer said the local market is thin early Friday. "Most people are sidelined. They're not sure whether speculators are still out there," he said. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rates is quoted at 7.25%, up from 5.5% late Thursday. The three-month rate is 11.5%, up from 10.75%. For more Hibor news, please refer to Telerate page [1085]. \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the six-month premium is quoted at 2,550 points, down from 2,650 late Thursday in Hong Kong, and also down from 2,700 overnight in London. The one-year premium is quoted at 5,000 points, down from 5,100 late Thursday both in Hong Kong and overnight in London. \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2802 7002; skennedy@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 07-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0149GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8706ox8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\p