\par\par \b \uc2  HK Late Hibor Mixed; HKMA Action Helps Overnight Rate Only \b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 1998\par 10:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong interbank rates were mixed late Thursday as the overnight rate responded to \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but the rest of the yield curve stubbornly refused to move. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 5.5%, down from 7.00% late Wednesday. The three-month rate is 10.75%, up from 10.625%. \par \par \uc2  A local dealer said banks are reluctant to lend, and the market remains thin. Dealers said the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's confirmation that it bought local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday has helped bring down the overnight rate, but longer term rates won't budge. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with an Australian bank said some institutions are still short-selling the Hong Kong dollar, which is casting a pall over sentiment. \par \par \uc2  A new rumor that the Hong Kong dollar peg to the U.S. dollar might be broken Monday when Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be closed for a market holiday is circulating even though dealers don't believe it. \par \par \uc2  "From a political point of view, there's no way they'd tamper with the peg right now. Maybe some time in the future (they might) but it all depends on the region's economies," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with a local bank. \par \par \uc2  Rumors about devaluation of the Chinese yuan have also been circulating in the market, dealers said. Both rumors are largely discounted, dealers added. \par \par \uc2  In the futures market, the September three-month Hibor contract is quoted at 88.70 for an underlying money market rate of 11.3%. It moved between 88.70, with an underlying rate of 11.30% and 89.20, with a yield of 10.8% on turnover of 1,885 lots, still well down on the 3,770 contracts traded in the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 06-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0853GMT \par \par \uc2  1085 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8606oz6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
