\par\par \b \uc2  HKMA Says Its HK Dlr Buying Wed Wasn't Market  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 180 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 1998\par 05:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday it wouldn't deem its market activity during the previous session as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at defending the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I wouldn't make that value judgment," a spokeswoman for the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  But the spokeswoman backed off of assertions made Wednesday that the authority bought local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the government put in requests for funds, amending her comments Thursday to say the HKMA acted in anticipation of a government request for funding. \par \par \uc2  The Wednesday transactions, which kept the Hong Kong dollar from weakening beyond HK$7.7505, came on a day when large U.S. investment banks were short-selling six-month and one-year Hong Kong dollar forward contracts. \par \par \uc2  Market participants have named several banks acting on behalf of Soros Fund Management and another hedge fund. Named banks included Morgan Stanley, which declined comment, and Merrill Lynch, which didn't reply to several phone calls seeking comment. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 06-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0327GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8606nza\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
