\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Weakens Slightly In London As Speculation Continues \b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 1998\par 12:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar has weakened to HK$7.7500 into the London trading session Thursday, with speculative forward activity that started in Asia continuing in the European trading day. \par \par \uc2  Around 1015 GMT, the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.501 against the U.S. dollar, compared with HK$7.7499 late Wednesday. Though the absolute movement isn't great, HK$7.7500 is typically the level at which the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps into the market to cool the U.S. dollar. Keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around HK$7.7500 are three large banks believed to be holding Hong Kong dollar buy orders for the HKMA at that level. The HKMA acted on its own Wednesday, buying the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the market, though it claimed it wasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  During the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading day Thursday, speculators continued to sell short the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the six-month and one-year forward markets, causing banks to tighten lending and rates to rise. The activity also kept pressure on the spot exchange rate and held it close to HK$7.7500. \par \par \uc2  Traders deemed the activity speculative in nature, with investors trying to force the spot rate weaker so that they could cover short forward positions at a profit. That's continuing in London, said a dealer there. \par \par \uc2  "We're seeing the usual crew that would be in the market when there's speculation going on," he said. "I think it could only be viewed as speculative positioning." \par \par \uc2  The dealer noted that trading in London is active, but the transaction size is small - about US$10 million to US$20 million per deal - so that market volume isn't tremendous. \par \par \uc2  He also said that forward positioning continues, but there's not much more of a surge from Asian trading. The six-month premium is up at 2700 points from 2650 points late in Asia and 2250 points late Wednesday. The one-year premium is 5100 points, steady from Asia and up from 4800 points above the spot rate late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Adam Najberg; (852)2802-7002; naj@asiaonline.net \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 06-08-98 \par \par \uc2  1058GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8606n0v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
