\par\par \b \uc2  HK$ Bond Prices Dn Late On Weak HK$, Rumors; 5-Yr Yld 9.87% \b0\par\par\uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 1998\par 11:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong bond prices fell again Wednesday as the Hong Kong dollar weakened to around HK$7.75 to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a level known to provoke \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Late Wednesday, the five-year Exchange Fund note was bid at 98.30, down from 98.90 late in the previous session, for a yield to maturity of 9.87%. Two-year notes fell to 97.00, from 97.38 late Tuesday, for a yield of 9.69%. \par \par \uc2  The yield curve for bills with a tenor of one year and shorter was virtually flat late in the session, with one-week, one-month and three-month bills all bid at 9.00%. \par \par \uc2  "The environment we have now is not that favorable," said a bond trader at a Chinese bank, citing the weak Hong Kong dollar, Tuesday's dramatic drop on Wall Street and persistent rumors that China will devalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "In the days to come, I would expect the Renminbi devaluation rumors (will have) to be cleared before we have the interest rates come down," the trader said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at HK$7.7495 late Wednesday, weaker than the HK$7.7483 recorded late in the previous session. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate was quoted at 7.00%, up from 6.50% late Tuesday. The three-month rate was 10.625%, up from 9.25% \par \par \uc2  For more information on Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market activity, bill and note prices and other related information, please refer to Telerate page [9888]. \par \par \uc2  -By Jeffrey Timmermans; (852) 2802-7002; jeffrey.timmermans@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 05-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0944GMT \par \par \uc2  4178 5096 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8506o37\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
