\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Late Hovers Near Key Support Level, Fwds Up \b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 1998\par 10:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar was weaker late Wednesday as the market braced itself for a possible round of selling out of New York and London overnight. \par \par \uc2  Around 0810 GMT (4:10 a.m. EDT), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7492 against the U.S. dollar, weaker than the HK$7.7483 quoted late Tuesday. The local unit has traded between HK$7.7490 and HK$7.7497 so far Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the spot Hong Kong dollar market is active, in contrast to the money market, where the local unit's weakness and a surge in interbank rates is keeping most players sidelined. \par \par \uc2  One dealer said he expects to see buying of the U.S. dollar and selling of the local unit overnight in New York and London, where the markets are thinner and easier to move. \par \par \uc2  Another local dealer said she expects to see some banks trying to push the spot Hong Kong dollar through HK$7.7500 per U.S. dollar, seen as a trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A rumor from Singapore questioning the viability of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar peg is also upsetting a skittish market, even though the government has repeatedly said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will remain pegged to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 7.00%, up from 6.50% late Tuesday. The three-month rate is 10.625%, up from 9.25%. For more Hibor news, please refer to Telerate page [1085]. \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the three-month premium is quoted at 1,050 points, up from 740 points previously. The six-month premium is quoted at 2,250 points, up from 1,730. The one-year premium is quoted at 4,400 points, up from 4,100 previously. \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2802 7002; skennedy@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 05-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0832GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8506nru\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
