\par\par \b \uc2  HK Hibor Sharply Higher Early On Speculative Fears \b0\par\par\uc2 236 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 1998\par 04:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong interbank rates are sharply higher early Wednesday amid growing fears that the Hong Kong dollar is ripe for another speculative attack. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 7.25%, compared with 6.5% late during the previous session. The three-month rate is 9.625% up from 9.25% late Tuesday. For more Hibor news, please refer to Telerate page [1085]. \par \par \uc2  A local bank treasurer said attention will be focused on the territory's stock market to see how it reacts to a 299.43-point fall on Wall Street overnight Tuesday and to the rise in local interbank rates early Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  He added that there's growing nervousness that speculators are massing to mount another assault on the Hong Kong dollar, noting that all the ingredients are correct. \par \par \uc2  Forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums have spiked, interbank rates are higher, the Hong Kong dollar is close to HK$7.7500 per U.S. dollar, a level believed to trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar has been sold for U.S. dollars by some U.S. institutions, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Early Wednesday, the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7498 per U.S. dollar, weaker than the HK$7.7483 recorded late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 05-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0208GMT \par \par \uc2  1085 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8506mie\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
