\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Steady Early, But Forwards Up On Liquidity Outflow \b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 1998\par 05:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar was steady early Monday, bolstered by higher interest rates, but forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums are up on selling of the local unit and continued Japanese yen fears. \par \par \uc2  Around 0310 GMT (11:10 p.m. Sunday EDT), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7478 per U.S. dollar, slightly stronger than the HK$7.7480 quoted late Friday. The local unit has traded between HK$7.7483 and HK$7.7485 so far Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Hong Kong dollar was sold overnight Friday at HK$7.7500, which is seen as a trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  As a result of the selling, there will be a HK$364.0 million fall in the aggregate balance, the accounts banks have with the HKMA to clear \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions. It will drop by 13.5% to HK$2.34 billion late Tuesday, when the transactions are settled. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there may have been further selling of the Hong Kong dollar which will only show up in the aggregate balance when, and if, the banks that bought Hong Kong dollars and sold U.S. dollars on-sell the Hong Kong dollars to the HKMA. \par \par \uc2  Forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums are rising, reflecting both the higher underlying money market rates following the outflow and concerns over the Japanese yen and Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the three-month premium is quoted at 640 points, compared with 590 points previously. The six-month premium is quoted at 1,600 points, up from 1,500. The one-year premium is quoted at 3,650 points, up from 3,500 previously. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 6.5%, up from 6.25% late Friday. The three-month rate is 8.75%, up from 8.625%. \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2802 7002; skennedy@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 27-07-98 \par \par \uc2  0343GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du7r06cdl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
