\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Firmer Late, Fwds Down On Japan PM Reform Hopes \b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 1998\par 10:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar was firmer late Tuesday amid increasing confidence that Japan's soon-to-be-named prime minister will have to undertake economic reform to revive demand and help the bank sector. \par \par \uc2  Around 0735 GMT (3:35 p.m. EDT), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7481 against the U.S. dollar, stronger than the HK$7.7486 quoted late Monday. The local unit has traded between HK$7.7484 and HK$7.7485 so far Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A local bank treasurer said banks believe that whoever is named Japan's prime minister Friday will have little option but to tackle reform. \par \par \uc2  "People believe that the new prime minister will have a new stabilization package for Japan," he said. \par \par \uc2  The spot Hong Kong dollar has made steady progress against the U.S. dollar, inching away from the sensitive HK$7.7500 level, which is seen as an trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's strength has helped bring down forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums. A dealer with a local bank said no one expects any significant movement in the Japanese yen against the U.S. dollar this week, or in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is helping the local unit. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 5.375%, compared with 5.5% late Monday. The three-month rate is 8.25%, down from 8.5%. For more Hibor news, please refer to Telerate page [1085]. \par \par \uc2  In the forward market, the three-month premium is quoted at 570 points, down from 620 points previously. The six-month premium is at 1,450 points, down from 1,550. The one-year premium is at 3,450 points, down from 3,650. \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2802 7002; skennedy@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-07-98 \par \par \uc2  0844GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du7l06594\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
