\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Early Unchanged, Still Flirts With Key Level \b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 1998\par 05:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar was calm early Thursday, hovering near a key support level in lackluster trade, and forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums are steady, suggesting speculators are sidelined. \par \par \uc2  Around 0300 GMT (11:00 p.m. EDT Wednesday), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.74903 per U.S. dollar, unchanged from late Wednesday. It has traded between HK$7.7490 and HK$7.7493 so far Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Despite the local unit's narrow range and lack of volatility, dealers said its current level concerns them. \par \par \uc2  "The TT (spot Hong Kong dollar) is trading on the high side, very close to HK$7.7500," said a dealer with an Australian institution. The HK$7.7500 level is seen as a trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The normally volatile forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is quiet, however, suggesting that noone is interested in building up big speculative positions at the moment. \par \par \uc2  In the forward market, the three-month premium is quoted at 560 points, up from 530 points previously. The six-month premium is at 1,520 points, down from 1,550. The one-year premium is unchanged at 3,600 points. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 6.0%, unchanged from late Wednesday. The three-month rate is 8.5%, up from 8.25%. For more Hibor news, please refer to Dow Jones [page 1085]. \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; 852 2802 7002; skennedy@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jone