\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Late Near Key Support Level; Banks Eye Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 1998\par 10:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar was barely changed late Monday as all eyes focused on the Japanese yen in the wake of Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto's resignation. \par \par \uc2  Late Monday, the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7495 per U.S. dollar, weaker than the HK$7.7492 recorded late Friday. The Hong Kong dollar has traded in a range of HK$7.7490 and HK$7.7495 so far Monday. \par \par \uc2  "Spot (Hong Kong dollar) is steady. There's been no activity so far," said a dealer with a local bank. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer with an Australian bank said: "there's more reason to do nothing than to do something." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said banks are waiting for signs of progress on Japanese financial reform and for indications of a medium-term trend in the yen. No one expects the Hong Kong dollar to come under pressure now because it's already close to HK$7.7500, which is seen as a trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  There's limited upward movement in the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market which is seen as more likely to be hedging than speculative, because the rises are smaller than the spikes that occurred on fund buying in recent months. \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the three-month premium is quoted at 730 points, up from 700 previously. The six-month premium is quoted at 1825 points, up from 1,800. The one-year premium is quoted at 4,200 points, up from 4,100 previously. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 5.00%, up from 4.50% late Friday. The three-month rate is 9.125%, down from 9.25%. \par \par \uc2  For more Hibor news, please refer to Dow Jones page \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2802 7002; skennedy@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 13-07-98 \par \par \uc2  0853GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du7d05wxa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
