\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Barely Changed Late; Forwards Surge On Yen Fears \b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 1998\par 12:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar shrugged off fears that the yen may test new support levels soon, but forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums surged. \par \par \uc2  Around 0630 GMT (2:30 a.m. EDT), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7492 against the U.S. dollar, a touch weaker than the HK$7.7490 late Thursday. The local unit has traded in a narrow range between HK$7.7492 and HK$7.7494. \par \par \uc2  While the Hong Kong dollar is range-bound - although close to HK$7.7500, which is seen as a trigger level for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums are rising on buying by U.S. banks and offshore funds. \par \par \uc2  The three-month premium is quoted at 700 points, compared with 570 points previously. The six-month premium is quoted at 1,800 points, up from 1,600. The one-year premium is quoted at 4,100 points, up from 3,800 previously. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar is bolstered by higher rates, resulting from a shrinkage in the aggregate balance, the accounts banks maintain with the HKMA to clear \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions. It will drop to HK$2.71 million late Monday as a result of selling of the Hong Kong dollar, after staying at HK$3.48 billion since late June. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rates is quoted at 5.75%, compared with 5.625% late during the previous session. The three-month rate is 9.125%, up from 8.25% late Thursday. For more Hibor news, please refer to Dow Jones [page 1085]. \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (85