\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Weaker Midday; US$ Demand Picks Up Ahead Of 2Q-End \b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 1998\par 06:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is weaker at midday Monday, with overseas investors selling due to genuine commercial U.S. dollar need before the end of the second quarter. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is quoted at HK$7.7495 per U.S. dollar at 0405 GMT (12:05 a.m. EDT), weaker than the HK$7.7485 level quoted late Friday. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a European bank said overseas investors, primarily from Japan, are exiting Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets to repatriate funds to Japan ahead of end of the quarter and the half-year. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar's rise is about over for the day, the dealer noted, with participants fearing that any more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-selling will prompt \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  at HK$7.7500. \par \par \uc2  As such, some investors who want to remain in the Hong Kong markets longer-term are seeking U.S. dollar funding through the swaps and forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Forward premiums opened lower than Friday's late levels, but have been climbing all morning. \par \par \uc2  Concerns that the Hong Kong dollar will face another speculative attack shortly before markets here close Wednesday for the one-year anniversary of the territory's return to Chinese rule have subsided. \par \par \uc2  The three-month forward premium is 870 points over the spot rate, compared with 900 points late Friday. The six-month premium is at 2200 ponits, flat from Friday and the one-year premium is down a touch to 5000 points from 5200 points. \par \par \uc2  Premiums will continue to edge higher Monday, but there won't be a nervous spike, as happened on Friday, the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  -By Adam Najberg; (852) 2802-7002; naj@asiaonline.net \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 29-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0430GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6t05hzp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
