\par\par \b \uc2  HK Late Hibor Falls On Rising Liquidity; Jitters Remain \b0\par\par\uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 1998\par 11:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong interbank rates fell late Monday as liquidity flowed back into the system and as a result of suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 6.00%, down from 8.00% late Friday. The three-month rate is 9.00%, down from 9.5% late Friday \par \par \uc2  Dealers said short-term interbank rates are falling as a result of the rises in aggregate balance, a key indicator of banking liquidity, which was at a low of HK$500 million Thursday. It's expected to jump to HK$2.59 billion later Monday, and to HK$3.47 billion later Tuesday as a result of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions. \par \par \uc2  They said the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the territory's quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has also been making money available. "The HKMA has injected liquidity through open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The increase in the balance and the rising short-term liquidity have marginally improved sentiment, but attention is still focused on the Japanese yen, dealers said. Another weakening of the yen would have an immediate spillover effect on the Hong Kong dollar and local rates. \par \par \uc2  Around 0815 GMT (4:15 a.m. EDT), the yen was quoted at Y138.55 against the U.S. dollar, compared with Y135.83 in New York late Friday. \par \par \uc2  In the futures, the three-month September Hibor contract is quoted at 89.35 for an underlying money market rate of 10.65%. It's traded between 89.35 (10.65%) and 89.84 (10.16%) on volume of 350 lots. \par \par \uc2  Late Monday, the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7417 per U.S. dollar, unchanged from late Friday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 22-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0909GMT \par \par \uc2  1085 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6m056m5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
