\par\par \b \uc2  US/HK forwards barely move by midday. \b0\par\par\uc2 662 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 1998\par 06:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab   MIDDAY\tab \tab   Open\tab    Previous Close\par HK$ SPOT\tab 7.7412/22\tab      7.7410/20    7.7405/30\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORWARDS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   3-Month     650-750\tab \tab  670-720\tab 650-750\par 6-Month     1,600-1,800\tab    1,500-1,800  1,525-1,725\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INTERBANK RATE (IN PERCENT)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overnight   6.75-7.62\tab      6.75-7.75    7.0-8.0\par 3-Month     8.25-9.37\tab      8.37-9.50    8.37-9.37\par 6-Month     9.12-10.25\tab     9.25-10.25   9.12-10.12.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, June 22 (Reuters) - US/HK forwards were mostly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par steady at midday on Monday from their opening levels but an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par upside bias remained strong amid volatility in the Japanese yen,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar was quoted at 137.52/54 yen at Tokyo midday,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par compared with last Friday's New York low of 133.60 yen, after a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weekend meeting of financial officials from Group of Seven (G7)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and Asian nations failed to boost confidence in the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Trading was quiet in the local money market in the absence\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of fresh market-moving news, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Since interbank rates have come down quite sharply over the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par past week after the U.S.-Japan joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen, we don't seen much downside from here," a senior dealer at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a U.S. based bank said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "But fresh bad news could push up rates any time, so the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bias is still on the upside," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The benchmark three-month interbank offered rate dropped to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 9.19 percent at Monday's fixing (GMT 0330) from a six-month high\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 16.26 quoted a week ago when the Japanese yen hovered between\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 145-147 per U.S. dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said key support for longer-dated rates was seen at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around eight percent in the near term if the yen stabilised at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the current level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) said local interest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates were likely to remain high until confidence returned to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par banking systems of the territory and the region, a newspaper\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reported on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If the degree of confidence is high, there won't be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par speculation and all that, and interest rates will come down to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par levels nearer to U.S. dollar interest rates," HKMA chief\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par executive Joseph Yam told the Hong Kong Standard.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said there had to be concerted efforts by central banks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the region to prevent the yen from falling to critical levels\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par again after it had stabilised on the back of the U.S.-Japan\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Since the U.S.-Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the yen last\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday, demand for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar has risen sharply,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The HKMA's page on the Reuters screen (HKMAOOB) showed that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the aggregate balance of net Hong Kong dollar sales for U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars has declined dramatically over the past week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "That means there is an inflow of funds," an HKMA spokesman\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said, adding there is an increased demand for the Hong Kong\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar against the U.S. dollar in the local banking system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The forecast change in aggregate balance attributable to\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions for Tuesday settlement was a positive HK$875\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million. This compared with a negative HK$7.26 billion quoted in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par early trade last Monday for settlement the next day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Starting June 12, the HKMA has added on its Reuters page\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a forecast of changes in the aggregate balance of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par banks' clearing accounts with the HKMA attributable to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HKMA's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asked if the HKMA was giving speculators ammunition to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par attack the Hong Kong dollar by disclosing this information, Yam\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was quoted as saying:\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "No, one thing I am quite sure of -- had we not disclosed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the information, the selling pressure (on the Hong Kong dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on June 12) would have intensified over the weekend and extended\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to Monday and Tuesday."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2847 4039; Fax 2845 0636.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6m02d4x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
