\par\par \b \uc2  HK forwards, rates fall after yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 256 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 03:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab     Open\tab \tab   Close\par HK$ SPOT\tab   7.7447/57\tab    7.7444/54\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORWARDS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 3-Month\tab  550-650\tab \tab 925-1,025\par 6-Month\tab  1,400-1,600\tab   2,000-2,200\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INTERBANK RATE (IN PERCENT)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overnight     7-8\tab \tab    7-10\par 3-Month\tab  8-10\tab \tab   8.50-11.5\par 6-Month\tab  8.5-10.5\tab     8.75-11.75.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, June 18 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  forwards\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fell sharply after joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the U.S. Federal\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reserve and the Bank of Japan lifted the yen and eased \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pressure across Asia, dealers said on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yen was trading at 136.35 at 0112 GMT on Thursday after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par skyrocketing firmer as New York's session opened on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Hong Kong interbank interest rates also dropped, reaching\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par single digits across the curve.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Market sentiment improved a great deal today, thanks to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen, and we see a lot of money offers in the interbank market,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par not just from local banks, but also from foreign banks,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore banks," a dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The (Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) does not even need to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offer money to ease liquidity today," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  showed some good early gains on the back\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of the yen's overnight surge after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates could ease further as more\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par banks joined the trend, but downside was still limited because\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of expectations of yen's volatility.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - Angi Li (852) 2843 4039; Fax (852) 2845 0636\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - Email: hongkong.newsroom@reuters.com.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6i02r1i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
