\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS-HK peg pressure eases after yen firms. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Alison Leung \par \uc2 699 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 06:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , June 18 (Reuters) - Joint U.S.-Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen has eased pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar by helping interest rates stabilise, analysts said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "This has eased pressure, which will be very positive for the Hong Kong interest rate environment," said Dong Tao, economist at Credit Suisse First Boston. \par \par \uc2  Under Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is linked at a rate of HK$7.78 to the U.S. dollar with full U.S. dollar backing for all Hong Kong dollars in circulation. \par \par \uc2  This makes the peg impossible to break - but rates move sharply higher whenever the Hong Kong dollar comes under selling pressure, inflicting severe pain on the overall economy. \par \par \uc2  As the yen has declined, Hong Kong rates have soared. But on Thursday, rates steadied and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards fell as the yen firmed to 136.35 to the U.S. dollar compared to a high of 144.09 early on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The overnight lending rate eased to 5.75 percent on Thursday and the benchmark three-month rate was at 7.50/9.50 percent from 8.50/11.50 percent. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards also relaxed sharply, indicating a sharp fall in hedging activity. Forwards blew out from already high levels when the yen accelerated its fall last week. \par \par \uc2  A firmer tone in the yen has eased fears of another round of competitive devaluations across Asia, and the rising risk of a depreciation in the Chinese yuan. \par \par \uc2  Over the past few days, China has stepped up its rhetoric about the damage a weak yen would do to its trade and investment performance, and hinted at the risks of yuan instability. \par \par \uc2  The real economic links between Hong Kong and the mainland would make it difficult for the Hong Kong peg to hold if China devalued, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "It takes the pressure off China and as goes the U.S. dollar, so goes Hong Kong," said Eric Nickerson, managing director at Bank of America in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  "A weaker U.S. dollar will take some of the pressure off Hong Kong assets to deflate," he said. \par \par \uc2  The overnight shift in environment has persuaded analysts that deposit rates would remain unchanged at the Hong Kong Association of Banks meeting on Friday. The bankers meet each Friday to set official deposit rates. \par \par \uc2  No change in deposit rates means little chance of a prime rate increase - something that will allow many people and businesses in Hong Kong to breathe a little easier. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong's prime lending rate - the rate banks charge their best clients - has remained at 10 percent since March 30 with an average spread between prime and the benchmark three-month interest rate of about 100 basis points. \par \par \uc2  But rates have been so volatile that Nickerson said it was impossible to target the type of rate spread that might trigger a prime rate increase. \par \par \uc2  "In March and April we had HIBOR at 400 basis points below prime. Since May, that has diminished rather significantly. As of June we've started a spike that has put (Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate) above prime, but now we're coming down again," he said. "So the rates coming down would suggest that as pressure comes off... we're likely to go down to that 100-something below prime that we've averaged." \par \par \uc2  But some analysts cautioned that while the rebound in the yen had eased pressure on China's yuan, markets were still waiting for concrete action from Japan to convince them the yen was stable. \par \par \uc2  "The yen rose to above 137 this morning but whether it can stay at these levels will very much depend on Japan's moves in the next few days to improve its economy," said Shamus Mok, chief economist at Bank of East Asia. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will only have a short-term impact in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and for the longer term it seems that Japan still has no special measures that could stimulate its economy." \par \par \uc2  - Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6470; Fax (852) 2845 0636 \par \par \uc2  - Email: hongkong.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6i02k0a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
