\par\par \b \uc2  HK rates ease at midday, US/HK forwards steady. \b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 1998\par 06:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab     Midday\tab \tab  Open\tab     Close\par HK$ SPOT\tab 7.7434/44\tab    7.7440/45\tab  7.7425/45\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORWARDS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 3-Month\tab  1,000-1,200\tab  1,100-1,200     1,375-1,500\par 6-Month\tab  2,100-2,300\tab  2,150-2,350     2,550-2,750\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INTERBANK RATE (IN PERCENT)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overnight     7-10\tab \tab   6-9\tab \tab  8-11\par 3-Month\tab  8.5-11.5\tab     10-13\tab      11-14\par 6-Month\tab  8.5-11.5\tab     10-13\tab      10-13.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, June 17 (Reuters) - Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  forwards\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were steady on Wednesday after dropping sharply at the open as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the yen hovered around 143 to the U.S. dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Profit-taking interest was getting lower as many hedge\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par funds had cut their long positions in the past two days," a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par senior dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Traders were watching a possible visit to Japan by U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Summers is expected to deliver a strong message to Japanese\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par leaders, urging them to do more to revive their economy and to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par arrest the yen's slide.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yen was relatively stable on Wednesday, trading at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 143.53 to the U.S. dollar compared to Monday's high of 146.75.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     This helped Hong Kong interbank rates to ease. Dealers said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par more banks were offering to lend money on the back of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stronger yen, and taking advantage of higher rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Interbank rates have risen sharply since Friday, when the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hong Kong dollar, dented by the yen woes, came under heavy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par selling pressure in New York.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , allowing the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unit to hold on to its key support level of HK$7.75.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But dealers said interbank rates were unlikely to fall by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par more than 200 basis points from present levels, given the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par volatity surrounding the yen, as well as strong money demand\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ahead of end-of-month book closing.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - Angi Li (852) 2843 4039; Fax (852) 2845 0636\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - Email: hongkong.newsroom@reuters.com.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6h02s07\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
