\par\par \b \uc2  HK 3-Mo Hibor -3: Overnight Rate 12.0% Vs 8.5% \b0\par\par\uc2 202 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 1998\par 12:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Based on swaps, the volatile overnight rate has risen to 12.0%, up from 8.5% late Friday in local trade and from 6.0% late Thursday. The one-month rate is quoted at 17%, up from 11.75% late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rises follow sales of Hong Kong dollars in early trade London, where the less liquid market for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes it more volatile. \par \par \uc2  They said the activity appears to be driven by speculators in London. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar sales went through at HK$7.75, which is seen as a trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell U.S. dollars. \par \par \uc2  "I think it (the HKMA) will be very, very busy in London tonight," a dealer with a Hong Kong institution said. \par \par \uc2  The HKMA doesn't comment on its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  activities. \par \par \uc2  In recent months, the spot Hong Kong dollar has regularly tested HK$7.75 in London and New York trade after the territory's own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets have closed. \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2802 7002; skennedy@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 12-06-98 \par \par \uc2  1043GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6c05165\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
