\par\par \b \uc2  US/HK forwards end firmer but off highs. \b0\par\par\uc2 487 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 1998\par 10:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, June 11 (Reuters) - US/HK forwards ended sharply firmer but off the day's highs as the yen hovered at the weaker side of 141 to the U.S. dollar, dealers said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  After opening at 850-950 points, the three-month dollar forward touched a high of 1,600-1,800 points as the yen marched closer to 142 against the greenback, but it faded back to 1,175-1,325 in late trade as the yen rebounded technically. \par \par \uc2  The six-month ended flat versus the open at 2,300-2,500 but higher than 1,900-2,100 at Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar was at HK$7.7476/86 versus HK$7.7460/70 at the open and HK$7.7483/93 per U.S. dollar at the close. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they did not notice any aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA). \par \par \uc2  "It (HKMA) did not do much in the money market as far as today is concerned, though one of the note-issuing banks was heard offering overnight money. We don't know if it is acting on behalf of the HKMA or not," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said anticipation of a Hong Kong dollar outflow on Friday helped lift interbank rates. \par \par \uc2  The HKMA's page on Reuters showed a negative position of HK$4.12 billion for Friday. \par \par \uc2  "This is a forecast and that meant the banks collectively sold more Hong Kong dollar than the aggregate balance, and therefore there may be some tightness in the market tomorrow," a HKMA spokesman said. \par \par \uc2  The HKMA said on Thursday it has revised the HKMA page on Reuters to enhance the transparency of its market activities. \par \par \uc2  Starting Thursday, the HKMA page (HKMAOOB) provides a forecast of changes in the aggregate balance of banks' clearing accounts with the HKMA attributable to the HKMA's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions. \par \par \uc2  The forecast will enable market participants to anticipate changes in the liquidity conditions in the interbank market, the HKMA said. \par \par \uc2  Local term money rates surged in early trade in response to the weak yen and Indonesian rupiah and perceived tighter interbank liquidity. \par \par \uc2  But rates eased later as local banks offered funds, especially at the longer end, taking advantage of the higher interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate soared to 7.30-8.00 percent in early trade against its close of 7.00-8.00, but eased to 5.00-6.00 percent in late trade. \par \par \uc2  The three-month was quoted at 11.00-13.00 versus 12.00-12.50 at the open and Wednesday's close of 10.00-11.00 percent. The six-month was quoted at 10.50-12.50 versus 12-13 percent at the open and 10.00-11.00 at the close. \par \par \uc2  - Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2847 4039. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6b036eq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
