\par\par \b \uc2  US/HK forwards soar by midday on yen, rupiah fall. \b0\par\par\uc2 510 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 1998\par 06:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  USD/HKD 7.7483/93  OVERNIGHT 7.00-9.00 3MO HKD/USD DEPOSIT 689 \par \par \uc2  USD/IDR 13800/4100 3 MO SWAP 1250-1450 2YR HKD/USD SPREAD  441 \par \par \uc2  USD/JPY 141.79/89  6 MO SWAP 2450-2650 10YR HKD/USD SPARED 438 \par \par \uc2  ---------------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2      *US/HK forwards surged on Thursday morning before retreating \par \par \uc2  slightly at midday. Market liquidity was tight amid a weak yen \par \par \uc2  and after a plunge of the Indonesian rupiah, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      *"The rupiah dived to 14,900 to the U.S. dollar and the yen \par \par \uc2  slipped below 141.50, which put pressure on the Hong Kong \par \par \uc2  dollar," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2      *The Hong Kong dollar eased to HK$7.7483/93 at midday from \par \par \uc2  HK$7.7460/70 at the open but was off its low of HK$7.7495 in \par \par \uc2  early trade. \par \par \uc2      *Heavy demand from Japanese banks for T.T. (telegraphic \par \par \uc2  transfer) forwards pushed the one-month forward rate to a high \par \par \uc2  of 625-725 points before it steadied at 450-550 at noon. This \par \par \uc2  compared to its open of 400-450 and Wednesday's close of 325-425 \par \par \uc2  points. \par \par \uc2      The three-month forward quickly surged to a high of \par \par \uc2  1,600-1,800 points after opening at 850-950. It was quoted at \par \par \uc2  1,300-1,400 points at noon versus Wednesday's close of 900-1,050 \par \par \uc2  points. \par \par \uc2      The six month forward opened up 100 points at 2,300-2,500 \par \par \uc2  and was quoted at 2,400-2,500 at midday. \par \par \uc2      *Hong Kong Chief Executive Tung Chee-hwa said on Wednesday \par \par \uc2  the government would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock market, which \par \par \uc2  indicated \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  would need higher interest rates to defend \par \par \uc2  its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one Japanese bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2      *Dealers said an anticipation of a Hong Kong dollar outflow \par \par \uc2  on Friday helped lift interbank rates. \par \par \uc2      The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's page on Reuters showed a \par \par \uc2  negative position of HK$4.12 billion for Friday. "This is a \par \par \uc2  forecast and that meant the banks collectively sold more Hong \par \par \uc2  Kong dollars than the aggregate balance and therefore there may \par \par \uc2  be some tightness in the market tomorrow," a HKMA spokesman \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2      *The spread between Hong Kong Exchange Fund notes and U.S. \par \par \uc2  treasuries widened this morning following a sharp rise in local \par \par \uc2  interest rates. Dealers said U.S. Federal Reserve chairman Alan \par \par \uc2  Greenspan's relatively neutral comments lifted U.S. treasuries \par \par \uc2  overnight, which was partly responsible for the widening yield \par \par \uc2  gaps between U.S. and Hong Kong dollar bonds. \par \par \uc2      Greenspan said the Fed might have to raise interest rates if \par \par \uc2  demand were to exhibit few signs of abating noticeably, but that \par \par \uc2  as yet, there was no need for a tighter monetary policy to cool \par \par \uc2  the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2      *Hong Kong's three month interbank rate was at 11.50-12.00 \par \par \uc2  percent against the morning high of 15 percent and Wednesday's \par \par \uc2  close of 10.00-11.00. \par \par \uc2   - Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6369; Fax (852) 2845 0636 \par \par \uc2   - Email: hongkong.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \p