\par\par \b \uc2  WRAP: HK Stks Plunge On  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Fears, Tung Speech \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sean Kennedy \par \uc2 266 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 1998\par 12:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong's battered markets took another pounding Wednesday on worries over the weak yen, fears of a possible yuan devaluation and a speech by Chief Executive Tung Chee-hwa that participants viewed in a negative light. \par \par \uc2  Already weak in the morning on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related concerns, the stock market took a further hit in the afternoon, as interbank rates and forward premiums jumped after Tung pledged to defend the linked exchange rate system. \par \par \uc2  The pledge was taken seriously, with nervous banks tightening lending in the already tight money markets, because the spot Hong Kong dollar has weakened to a level that typically sees \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  After notching steady losses in morning trading, the blue-chip Hang Seng Index plummeted in the afternoon, ending down 4.9% at a three-year low of 7979.37, with overseas mutual funds dumping shares as they decreased their exposure to Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar weakened and flirted with a key support level of HK$7.750 all day. \par \par \uc2  Fears of a yuan devaluation rose after People's Bank of China Governor Dai Xianglong said Tuesday that China's exports and foreign investment inflow were being hurt by the weak Japanese yen. Dai also pledged that China won't devalue. \par \par \uc2  Despite that pledge, lingering worries about the yuan drove Hong Kong interbank interest rates close to double digits in the morning and caused forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  premiums to climb. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 10-06-98 \par \par \uc2  1058GMT \par \par \uc2  1134 4205 62555 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6a04ysh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
