\par\par \b \uc2  HK$ Bond Prices Dn -2: Mkts Spooked By Tung Comments \b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 1998\par 12:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  "One of the reasons is the dollar-yen rate, but during lunchtime we saw some transactions in the TT (spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market) near HK$7.75," said a trader at a Chinese bank. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  is known to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakens above HK$7.75 to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Around 0954 GMT (5:54 a.m. EDT), the Hong Kong dollar is trading at HK$7.7495 to the U.S. dollar, weaker than the HK$7.7485 recorded late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese yen, meanwhile, hit an intraday high of Y140.98 against the U.S. dollar, before strengthening to Y140.56 around 0955 GMT. \par \par \uc2  In addition, local markets were spooked by comments by Hong Kong chief executive Tung Chee-Hwa reiterating support for the Hong Kong dollar's peg to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite already tight liquidity in the territory's banking system. \par \par \uc2  Money market dealers said they interpreted Tung's comments to mean that the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  might soon squeeze interbank rates higher to strengthen the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment in the market continues to be very fragile, the bond trader at a Chinese bank added. "Anything is making people nervous," she said. \par \par \uc2  For more information on Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market activity, bill and note prices and other related information, please refer to Dow Jones page [9888]. \par \par \uc2  -