\par\par \b \uc2  HK's Hang Seng Index ends at three year low on yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 778 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 1998\par 10:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, June 10 (Reuters) - Hong Kong's Hang Seng Index was knocked back to its lowest close in more than three years on Wednesday as a weak yen sent investors on a selling spree, brokers said. \par \par \uc2  The Hang Seng Index ended down 412.09 points, or 4.91 percent, at 7,979.37, its lowest close since March 10, 1995. \par \par \uc2  The blue chip index earlier hit a low of 7,906.39, its lowest intra-day level since March 8, 1995, when it reached 7,905.75. \par \par \uc2  China plays were hit hard and the China-Affiliated Corporations Index shed 5.08 percent to 887.41 points while H shares dived 5.60 percent to 429.81. \par \par \uc2  Brokers said the weak yen continued to plague the market as the U.S. dollar climbed above 141 yen in Wednesday trade. \par \par \uc2  China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, Dai Xianglong, said on Tuesday the weak yen was having a severe impact on Beijing's foreign trade and brokers said the soft yen sparked concern about the strength of the Chinese yuan. \par \par \uc2  "Our current view is that the renminbi is relatively safe although there is a risk element of the yen," said Robert Sassoon, head of research at SG Securities. \par \par \uc2  "If the yen does depreciate - if it goes beyond 150 - then we will obviously review the situation." \par \par \uc2  Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  suffered a fairly severe thrashing as markets fretted about the yen, and most other regional stock markets were hammered lower. \par \par \uc2  In Thailand, stocks plunged more than five percent while share prices in Seoul lost more than four percent. \par \par \uc2  The development of the yen was expected to dictate market direction in the short term and investors were watching for further news from the Group of Seven meeting, brokers said. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers said senior officials from the G7 nations discussed the possible adverse effect of the yen's weakness on Wednesday and would continue to monitor developments in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  "I think the market is already discounting a yen at up to 145 (against the U.S. dollar)," said Percy Au-Young, sales director at DBS Securities. \par \par \uc2  Au-Young said a bearish scenario would give the Hang Seng Index a downside of 8,000 in the medium term but added a rebound in the yen may trigger the index to climb higher. \par \par \uc2  "There is a lot of value in the market but the question is what is going to trigger people to come back," Sassoon said. \par \par \uc2  "There should be an element of short-covering soon. The question is whether people are going to panic." \par \par \uc2  Sharply higher interest rates rocked sentiment and the benchmark three-month HIBOR rate rose to 9.57895 percent on Wednesday's fixing against 9.08750 percent at the same time on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate touched as high as seven to eight percent versus 5.50-6.00 at Tuesday's close. The three-month forward jumped to 1,000-1,200 points against 640-690 at Tuesday's close. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar weakened below the key support of HK$7.75 against the U.S. dollar at one point before bouncing back to HK$7.7483/93 in late trade. \par \par \uc2  Dealers cited rumours that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early trade to defend the support at 7.75. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong leader Tung Chee-hwa said on Wednesday his administration was determined to keep the Hong Kong dollar peg against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Tung said the Hong Kong dollar was under pressure due to the weak yen this week. \par \par \uc2  "Any deviation from our long-held philosophy of fiscal prudence will give rise to speculative attack against the Hong Kong dollar, the result of which may well be another increase in our interest rates," he said. \par \par \uc2  Lower futures added pressure to the market and the June Hang Seng Index contract erased 400 points to 7,960 with open interest remaining large at 80,678 contracts. The July contract finished down 370 points at 8,010. \par \par \uc2  Index heavyweight HSBC Holdings  accounted for more than a quarter of the Hang Seng Index point loss as it slumped HK$9.00 to HK$181.00. \par \par \uc2  Cheung Kong  dived HK$3.00 to HK$33.80 and Sun Hung Kai Properties eased HK$1.90 to HK$30.30. Hutchison  was off HK$2.50 at HK$34.00. \par \par \uc2  Investors awaited U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's testimony to Congress at 1500 GMT. \par \par \uc2  - Kristina Zetterlund (852) 2843 6358; Fax (852) 2845 0636 \par \par \uc2  - Email: hongkong.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  *. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6a03avv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
