\par\par \b \uc2  HK stocks sharply off at midday, shaken by yen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jennifer Genevieve \par \uc2 646 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 1998\par 07:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, June 10 (Reuters) - Hong Kong's Hang Seng Index sank to its lowest levels since mid-January on Wednesday morning, closing sharply lower at midsession as yen weakness and concerns about the Chinese yuan pushed prices into a tailspin. \par \par \uc2  The Hang Seng Index closed the morning session at 8,036.17 points, down 355.29 points, or 4.23 percent. \par \par \uc2  In China-related stocks, the red chip index sank even further, sliding 58.90 points, or 6.30 percent, to 876.02 while the H-share index fell 22.88 points, or 5.03 percent, to 432.42. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are at the forefront of everybody's mind. The market is obviously focused on a possible devaluation of the yuan," said Steven Thompson, chief analyst at Nikko Research Center. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar edged up against the yen in early afternoon trade in Tokyo. It was quoted at 140.83/88 yen and stop-loss dollar buying was expected to take place above 141.00 yen. \par \par \uc2  China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Dai Xianglong said on Tuesday the weak Japanese yen was having a severe impact on Beijing's foreign trade. H-share companies were getting particularly hard hit as they competed with Korean and Japanese producers in heavy industries, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "Obviously the weakness of the yen is a problem," said Richard Verin, head of equities trading at Credit Suisse First Boston. "There is obviously a bit of panic given some of the moves we have seen." \par \par \uc2  He said the selling of H shares and red chips was probably coming from local retail investors. \par \par \uc2  "It may be an indication that we are now getting to the stage where people are having to cut losses to generate new cash to meet whatever commitments they need to meet," said Thompson. \par \par \uc2  In the blue chip sector, investors were selling where there was liquidity, brokers said. \par \par \uc2  Swire Pacific Ltd ended the morning down HK$2.90 at HK$21.70, Cheung Kong (Holdings) Ltd fell HK$2.50 to HK$34.30 and HSBC Holdings Plc dropped HK$6.00 to HK$184.00. \par \par \uc2  "The market is on debt watch right now. There seem to be concerns about credit ratings at the moment," said Thompson. \par \par \uc2  Moody's Investors Service said this week it had placed its ratings on the debt of Swire Pacific and its guaranteed subsidiaries under review for possible downgrade. \par \par \uc2  Debt concerns also plagued Wharf (Holdings) Ltd which was down HK$0.70 at HK$7.60 and CITIC Pacific Ltd which fell HK$1.45 to HK$13.80. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the Hang Seng Index was now heading for a new year low. It ended just above the day's low of 8,007.04 points at midsession. \par \par \uc2  The 1998 low stands at 7,909.13, reached on January 12. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong interbank rates rose on Wednesday with the benchmark three-month HIBOR rate at 9.58 percent at the fixing compared with 9.09 percent at the same time on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar was at 7.7495/7.7505 to the U.S. dollar. \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said there was talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend key support at 7.75. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts said the situation was too uncertain around the region for investors to want to bargain hunt. But others said that those who had sold at higher levels would be tempted. \par \par \uc2  "There may be such a bounce that investors won't have a chance to accumulate at 8,000," said Thompson. \par \par \uc2  The June futures contract on the Hang Seng Index ended the morning down 310 points at 8,050, after falling to a low during the morning of 7,980 points. The July contract was off 340 points at 8,040. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6a03av6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
