\par\par \b \uc2  US/HK forwards extend gain, spot off key 7.75. \b0\par\par\uc2 409 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 1998\par 06:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  USD/HKD 7.7495/00   OVERNIGHT 6.00-6.50 3MO HKD/USD DEPOSIT 405 \par \par \uc2  USD/IDR 12200/12300 3MO SWAP  730-780   2YR HKD/USD SPREAD  388 \par \par \uc2  USD/JPY 140.83/0.93 6MO SWAP 1600-1800  10YR HKD/USD SPREAD 419 \par \par \uc2   -------------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2      *US/HK forwards extended sharp gains by midday, bids mainly \par \par \uc2  came from U.S. investment banks, dealers said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      *Dealers cited a rumor that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar against the greenback, defending key support at 7.75. \par \par \uc2      The Hong Kong dollar rebounded swiftly from HK$7.75 to \par \par \uc2  HK$7.7495/05 per U.S. dollar by midday, still weaker than \par \par \uc2  HK$7.7491/96 at the open and HK$7.7480/90 at the close. \par \par \uc2      Market nervousness intensified as the local stock market \par \par \uc2  plunged to a five-month low and interbank liquidity tightened in \par \par \uc2  the wake of a feeble yen and growing concerns over the possible \par \par \uc2  devaluation of the Chinese yuan. \par \par \uc2      The three-month forward was sharply firmer at 750-800 points \par \par \uc2  versus 700-750 at the open and 640-690 at the close. \par \par \uc2      The six-month was up at 1,700-1,850 versus 1,550-1,700 at \par \par \uc2  the open and 1,500-1,600 at the close. \par \par \uc2      The Liquidity Adjustment Facility reversal at the Hong Kong \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at HK$3.2 billion on Wednesday, \par \par \uc2  compared with some HK$4 billion over the past week, raising \par \par \uc2  renewed fears of a liquidity crunch, sending short term rates \par \par \uc2  firmer. \par \par \uc2      The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on the \par \par \uc2  market rumour about its possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2      "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is stable and we do not comment on \par \par \uc2  money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a spokeswoman from the HKMA said. \par \par \uc2      Local term money rates were firmer across the board. \par \par \uc2      The overnight rate rose to 6.25-6.75 percent versus \par \par \uc2  5.87-6.37 at the open and 5.50-6.00 at the close. The \par \par \uc2  three-month was indicated at 9.00-9.75 versus 8.93-9.25 at the \par \par \uc2  open and 8.50-9.00 at the close. The six-month was quoted at \par \par \uc2  9.75-10.12 versus 9.50-10.00 at the open and 9.00-9.50 at the \par \par \uc2  close. \par \par \uc2   -Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2847 4039. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6a03asp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
