\par\par \b \uc2  HK interbank rates jump as yen breaks 141. \b0\par\par\uc2 470 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 1998\par 09:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      HONG KONG, June 10 (Reuters) - Hong Kong interbank rates rose sharply in late Wednesday trade as nervousness intensified after the yen dipped below 141 per U.S. dollar and the local stock market plunged below 8,000 levels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      "The market has become rather panicky as the Japanese yen fell below 141," Toby Yuen, treasurer at Bank Brussels Lambert, said. \par \par \uc2      The overnight rate touched as high as seven to eight percent versus 5.87-6.37 at the open and 5.50-6.00 at Tuesday's close. \par \par \uc2      "But I did not notice any substantial sales against the Hong Kong dollar today," Yuen said. \par \par \uc2      Another senior dealer said: "As short term rates get firmer, the market gets more nervous." \par \par \uc2      Money market sources said they heard that some major speculators had re-emerged in the local money market taking short positions against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2      Dollar forwards moved higher and more rapidly \par \par \uc2  than in recent days. The three-month forward was up at \par \par \uc2  1,000-1,200 points versus 750-800 at midday, 700-750 at the open \par \par \uc2  and 640-690 at Tuesday's close. \par \par \uc2      The six-month rose to 1,900-2,100 versus 1,700-1,850 at \par \par \uc2  midday, 1,550-1,700 at the open and 1,500-1,600 at the close. \par \par \uc2      At one point in early trade on Wednesday, the Hong Kong \par \par \uc2  dollar weakened below the key support of HK$7.75 per U.S. dollar \par \par \uc2  before bouncing back to HK$7.7483/93 (GMT 0745) in late trade. \par \par \uc2      Dealers cited rumours that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in early trade, \par \par \uc2  buying the Hong Kong dollar against the greenback and defending \par \par \uc2  the support at 7.75. \par \par \uc2      The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on the \par \par \uc2  market rumour. \par \par \uc2      "The Hong Kong dollar is stable and we do not comment on \par \par \uc2  money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a spokeswoman from the HKMA told \par \par \uc2  Reuters on Wendesday. \par \par \uc2      But local interbank liquidity was tighter, raising renewed \par \par \uc2  fear of an upward bias for interbank rates. \par \par \uc2      The Liquidity Adjustment Facility reversal at the Hong Kong \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at HK$3.2 billion on Wednesday, \par \par \uc2  compared with some HK$4 billion over the past week. \par \par \uc2      Stephen Cheung, a director at Jardine Fleming Bank, said the \par \par \uc2  weakening yen would continue to provide the main direction for \par \par \uc2  local interbank rates. \par \par \uc2      "The situation is worrying. Now the interbank rates \par \par \uc2  (longer-dated) are trading above the prime rate," he said. \par \par \uc2      "But raising the prime rate seems impossible given the \par \par \uc2  current state of the economy," he said. \par \par \uc2      The three-month and the six-month were quoted in a similar \par \par \uc2  range of 10.00-11.00 percent in late trade versus the prime rate \par \par \uc2  of 10.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6a03apj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
