\par\par \b \uc2  HK stocks extend fall, Hang Seng hits new year low. \b0\par\par\uc2 457 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 1998\par 08:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, June 10 (Reuters) - Hong Kong stocks continued their slide on Wednesday afternoon and the Hang Seng Index hit a new year low, hammered by a weak Japanese yen, brokers said. \par \par \uc2  The Hang Seng Index opened afternoon trade down 5.05 percent at 7,968 points and quickly extended the fall to a new year low of 7,908 points, off 5.76 percent. \par \par \uc2  The blue chip index's previous low for 1998 was 7,909.13 which it reached on January 12. \par \par \uc2  "The market is just sinking and it is going to continue to sink for the time being because there is very limited buying interest out there, if any," said Johan Tellvik, sales director at Caspian Securities. \par \par \uc2  "We have broken through 8,000 so I would assume the next support level would be somewhere around 7,500." \par \par \uc2  China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Dai Xianglong said on Tuesday the weak Japanese yen was having a severe impact on Beijing's foreign trade and brokers said there was concern the weak yen would put pressure on the yuan. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong leader Tung Chee-hwa said on Wednesday the Hong Kong dollar was under pressure due to the weak yen this week. \par \par \uc2  "Any deviation from our long-held philosophy of fiscal prudence will give rise to speculative attack against the Hong Kong dollar, the result of which may well be another increase in our interest rates," Tung said. \par \par \uc2  Higher interbank rates hurt sentiment as the U.S. dollar climbed above 141 yen. The three-month HIBOR rate rose to 9.57895 percent at Wednesday's fixing against 9.08750 percent at the same time on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar was trading at HK$7.7475/00 against the U.S. dollar compared to HK$7.7480/90 at Tuesday's close. \par \par \uc2  Dealers cited a rumour that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar against the greenback, defending key support at 7.75. \par \par \uc2  Tung Chee-hwa will hold a news conference on Wednesday at 3.45 pm (0745 GMT), the government information service said. \par \par \uc2  China plays were hit hard and the China-Affiliated Corporations Index shed 5.44 percent to 884.05 while H-shares dropped 5.93 percent to 428.31. \par \par \uc2  Index heavyweight HSBC Holdings  dived HK$8.50 to HK$181.50. Cheung Kong  slid HK$2.80 to HK$34.00 and Sun Hung Kai Properties  was down HK$1.90 at HK$30.30. \par \par \uc2  Hutchison  was off HK$2.40 at HK$34.10. \par \par \uc2  - Kristina Zetterlund (852) 2843 6358; Fax (852) 2845 0636 \par \par \uc2  - Email: hongkong.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  *. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6a03aik\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
