\par\par \b \uc2  HK Late Hibor Rates Edge Off Highs, Get Ready For New Round \b0\par\par\uc2 257 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 1998\par 10:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong interbank rates edged down late Monday after profit-taking in the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but dealers say sentiment remains bleak. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 5.125%, up from 4.75% late Friday, but well down on the 6.5% quoted early Monday. The three-month rate is 9.00%, down from 8.625% late Friday, but down on 9.25% early Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the intraday fall is being driven by the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, which spiked earlier in the day after the yen pushed through 140 yen against the U.S. dollar, undermining other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Sentiment is quite bearish. We just had a limited rebound on profit-taking," said a dealer with an Australian bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers don't see scope for significant further falls in local rates, while Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are being led downward by the Japanese yen, particularly not while the Hong Kong dollar is so close to HK$7.75. This is seen as a trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  As with last week, banks are generally unwilling to lend while the sentiment is so bad, and are sitting on cash. This is keeping upward pressure on interbank rates. \par \par \uc2  Late Monday, the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7487 per U.S. dollar, stronger than the HK$7.7497 recorded late Friday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 08-06-98 \p