\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Approaches Danger Point Late As Speculators Circle \b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 1998\par 11:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar pushed toward a key support level late Friday after Japanese yen weakness and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jitters unnerved the local market. \par \par \uc2  At 1655 GMT (4:55 a.m. EDT), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7498 against the U.S. dollar, up from HK$7.7492 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  That's perilously close to the HK$7.75 level which is believed to trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the territory's quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said rumors that at least one fund is pushing up forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates and that the Tiger fund sold Hong Kong government debt to put pressure on the money market is pushing the local unit upwards. \par \par \uc2  They said funds appear to be exploiting nervousness over a weak Japanese yen, which has spilled over to affect other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "Speculators are out there taking positions," said a dealer with a local bank. \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the one-month is quoted at 170 points from 140 late in the previous session. The three-month premium is quoted at 620 points, compared with 550 points. The six-month premium is quoted at 1450 points, up from 1300 previously. The one-year premium is quoted at 3400 points, up from 3250 previously. \par \par \uc2  "The big players from Singapore are bidding up the market," said a dealer from a European bank. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 4.75%%, down from 5.0% late Thursday. The benchmark three-month rate is 8.625%, up from 8.25%. \par \par \uc2  For more Hibor news, please refer to Dow Jones page \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2802 7002; skennedy@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 05-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0944GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6504tzi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
