\par\par \b \uc2  HK Late Hibor Up On  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Fears; Banks Hoard Cash \b0\par\par\uc2 282 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 1998\par 10:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong longer-term interbank rates rose late Friday as renewed speculation fears weakened the Hong Kong dollar and banks stopped lending anything but short-term money. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 4.75%%, down from 5.0% late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "I heard about a huge fund which was selling in government bonds from five years to 10 years," said a local bank dealer, referring to the Tiger fund, which has been tipped as a major player in the Hong Kong dollar market in the past. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said the selling pushed 10-year bond yields up 40 basis points, and hit longer-term interbank rates. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark three-month rate is 8.625%, up from 8.25% late Thursday, and the six-month rising to about 9.5% late Friday, from about 8.75%. previously. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said banks that were already reluctant to lend past one or two months now won't lend past those maturities until the market settles. \par \par \uc2  The sight of the Japanese yen breaking back through 139 yen to the U.S. dollar sparked fears of more Asian contagion, and the Hong Kong dollar has traded dangerously close to the support point of HK$7.75, which is believed to trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The HKMA, \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , doesn't comment on the level of the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  Late Friday, the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7497 per U.S. dollar, weaker than the HK$7.7492 recorded late Thursday. \par \pa