\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Near Key Support Level Late; Forwards Renew Rise \b0\par\par\uc2 401 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 1998\par 11:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar Monday continued to flirt with a key support level that's generally believed to trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Around 0900 GMT (5 a.m. EDT), the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is quoted at HK$7.7497 per U.S. dollar, weaker than the HK$7.7495 recorded late Friday. It's very close to HK$7.75, believed to be an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level for the HKMA, although the HKMA doesn't comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar has traded in a range of HK$7.7495 and HK$7.7498 so far Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said spot Hong Kong dollar trading was relatively quiet Monday, with most of the activity concentrated in the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market where an unnamed U.S. institution is believed to be building up a position. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with an Australasian institution said the activity appeared to be a continuation of four days of buying in the forward market last week, apart from a brief downward blip Friday. \par \par \uc2  He said the U.S. institution resumed buying in the forward market when London opened Friday, and forwards rose in Hong Kong on Monday as a result. \par \par \uc2  While few believe that a speculative attack on the Hong Kong dollar could succeed, there are continued fears of a squeeze in the money market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Indonesia, whose markets were closed for a public holiday Monday, is also a nagging concern, and further unrest in Indonesia would bring the Hong Kong dollar under pressure and push forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates up further. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 4.875%, up from 4.50% late Friday. The three-month rate is 7.125% up from 7.00% late Friday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For more Hibor news, please refer to Dow Jones\par page [1085].\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the forward \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, the one-month rate is quoted\par at 100 points, up from 85 late in the previous session. The three-month\par premium is quoted at 320 points, compared with 290 points previously.\par The six-month premium is quoted at 920 points, up from 800 previously.\par The one-year premium is quoted at 2,600 points, up from 2,200.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2802 7002;\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sean.kennedy@cor.dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 11-05-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0913GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5b03xtn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
