\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Steady Near HK$7.75/Dlr Midday, No  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 343 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 1998\par 07:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is slightly weaker midday Friday, hovering near HK$7.75 to the U.S. dollar, a level known to trigger buying of U.S. dollars by the territory's quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Around 0445 GMT (12:45 a.m. EDT), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7492 against the U.S. dollar, slightly weaker from HK$7.7490 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  'It's pretty close to HK$7.75, but at the moment I don't think it will go any weaker,' said a trader at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  Weakness in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , centered around the Indonesian rupiah, is putting pressure on the Hong Kong dollar, traders say. \par \par \uc2  U.S. hedge funds are also reported to have descended upon Asia again, and a Hong Kong Chinese-language newspaper reported Friday that U.S. hedge fund manager Julian Robertson's Tiger Fund has taken on a US$1.0 billion position, betting on an interest rate rise in the territory \par \par \uc2  A local bank treasurer noted some selling of Hong Kong dollars for U.S. dollars by Chinese banks, but not in sufficient volumes to push the spot rate past HK$7.75. \par \par \uc2  Market participants report that, so far, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't been seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 4.875% by Standard Chartered Bank, up from 4.125% late Thursday. For more Hibor news, please refer to Dow Jones page [1085]. \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, premiums have declined slightly after Thursday's sharp rise. The one-month is quoted at 85 points from 100 late in the previous session. The three-month premium is quoted at 320 points, compared with 330 points previously. The six-month premium is quoted at 850 points, down from 950 previously. \par \par \uc2  -By Jeffrey Timmermans; (852)2802-7002; \par \par \uc2  jeffrey.timmermans@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-05-98 \par \par \uc2  0513GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5803ume\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
