\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Lower Early, Flirts With Key Support Level \b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 1998\par 06:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar weakened further Wednesday morning and edged closer to the key support level, sparking concerns that interest rates might be squeezed up. \par \par \uc2  Around 0415 GMT (12:15 a.m. EST), the Hong Kong dollar was quoted at HK$7.7493 against the U.S. dollar, down from HK$7.7489 late Tuesday. The Hong Kong dollar traded in a narrow range between HK$7.7487 and HK$7.7493 so far Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  'The falling stock market reflects a general bearishness. And (as the) \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is leaning so close to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level of HK$7.750, people are wary that rates may be increased later,' said a dealer at a Chinese bank. \par \par \uc2  The Hang Seng index fell through the key level of 10,000 early in the morning and recovered later. Still, it ended the morning session down 154.13 points. \par \par \uc2  Dealers are convinced that the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , will step in if the local dollar weakened further. \par \par \uc2  The jittery sentiment sent higher interbank market rates and premiums in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the one-month is quoted at 28, up from 20 late Tuesday. The three-month premium is quoted at 180 points, compared with 160 points previously. The six-month premium is quoted at 620 points, up from 600. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate is quoted at 4.75%, compared with 4.25% late in the previous session. The three-month rate is 6.4375%, up from 6.375%. \par \par \uc2  For more Hibor news, please refer to Dow Jones page \par \par \uc2  -By Noel Fung; (852) 2802 7002;noel.fung@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 06-05-98 \par \par \uc2  0455GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5603saa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
