\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Slightly Lower Late; Investors Move Into US Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Mai 1998\par 12:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is a touch lower late Friday from Thursday, with market players tending to switch to the U.S. dollar ahead of the weekend. \par \par \uc2  At 0955 GMT (5:35 a.m. EDT), the Hong Kong dollar is trading at HK$7.7483 per U.S. dollar from HK$7.7470 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar is usually weaker on Fridays, as investors prefer holding the U.S. dollar ahead of the weekend. This week the U.S. dollar is especially attractive because U.S. dollar interbank rates are higher than comparable Hong Kong dollar rates. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong interbank rates fell back to normal levels Thursday after money market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  and have been stable Friday, as market liquidity has been restored by the HKMA. \par \par \uc2  'As many (banks) are long on Hong Kong dollar...rates can fall back quickly on short-term - one or two days - demand only,' said a treasury head of a domestic bank. \par \par \uc2  Trading in both the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and forward markets is mostly quiet, as many Asian and European financial markets are closed for a public holiday Friday. \par \par \uc2  The spot 'TT,' is in 'featureless trading' Friday, said the treasury head, referring to the U.S. dollar-Hong Kong dollar exchange rate. Only Hong Kong and Japan are open in the region, and most European markets, except London, are closed. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with an Asian bank said the spot Hong Kong dollar traded in a narrow range between HK$7.7478 and HK$7.7485 Friday in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  In the forward market, the one-month premium is at 20 points over the spot rate, down from 35 points late Thursday. The three-month premium is also down to 160 points from late Thursday's 180 points. \par \par \uc2  The six-month premium is quoted at 570 points, down from 600 points late Thursday and early Friday. \par \par \uc2  -By Daisy S.Y. Wong; 852-2802-7002; dwong@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 01-05-98 \par \par \uc2  1037GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5103oq9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
