\par\par \b \uc2  ASIAN EXOTICS - Ringgit, won shed gains. \b0\par\par\uc2 717 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  0515 GMT - The Malaysian ringgit slipped a bit after Singapore denied rumours it had agreed to buy land owned by Malaysia's state railway company for 30 billion ringgit. \par \par \uc2  * A spokesman for Singapore Prime Minister Goh Chok Tong's office told Reuters there was no truth to the reports, which surfaced in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Wednesday and contributed to the ringgit's rise. \par \par \uc2  * But dealers said the ringgit was relatively resilient despite the denial of the rumours and Kuala Lumpur's apparent rejection of an IMF call for higher Malaysian interest rates in its recent annual review of the economy. \par \par \uc2  * Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad on Wednesday defended Malaysia's stance of keeping interest rates at current levels, saying businesses were already suffering. \par \par \uc2  * Bank Negara Malaysia accepted bids for one-month money at an average 11.04 percent and three-month at 11.07 percent under a new competitive bidding system, aimed at increasing transparency. \par \par \uc2  * The Indonesian rupiah remained stuck below the 8,000 level, ignoring economic czar Ginandjar Kartasasmita's confidence-boosting comments. \par \par \uc2  * Ginandjar said the rupiah should regain the 6,000 per dollar level this year if economic reforms remain on track, and expressed confidence this would be the case. \par \par \uc2  He said fuel and electricity prices would go up in May and all subsidies, except for rice and soybeans, would be abolished by October 1 as per the IMF agreement. \par \par \uc2  Ginandjar also announced a 15 percent pay increase for civil servants from May 1, conceding that this did not match inflation which jumped more than 25 percent in the first quarter. \par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sjahril Sabirin said overnight that interest rates would stay high for the time being to support the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  * But dealers said the forward market was already pricing higher interest rates and spot rupiah was unlikely to perk up against a backdrop of continuing social tension and signs of a slowdown in IMF funding. \par \par \uc2  * A senior IMF official said the fund would make its next proposed $3 billion payment to Indonesia in three installments and added that the fund had misjudged the crisis in its early stage. \par \par \uc2  * In South Korea, the won slid from its high of 1,326 as private and state-run companies aggressively tried to hedge their dollar exposures in forward trading on a belief the equilibrium for the exchange rate was at 1,350/1,400. \par \par \uc2  * News of soaring inflation, yet more worrying evidence of the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis, did not help the market. The producer price index soared 17.5 percent year-on-year in April, against a 3.8 percent rise the year before. The consumer price index was up 8.8 percent year-on-year in April against a 4.3 percent the year before. \par \par \uc2  * The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said April import prices fell 9.1 percent month-on-month in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  terms, but rose 34.3 percent on a yearly basis. Export prices fell 11.7 month-on-month and rose 34.1 percent year-on-year. \par \par \uc2  * The Thai baht was weak as the market turned apprehensive about its recent rally amid signs the government might not want it to strengthen further. \par \par \uc2  * Deputy Prime Minister Supachai Panitchpakdi said overnight he was happy with an exchange rate of 40 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  * "I don't see the baht continuing to strengthen from here once the buying euphoria is over. But we could see continuous (dollar) sell offers if there is more investment in Thai companies," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  * A Thai newspaper reported that a government-appointed panel probing the Bank of Thailand had blamed several senior finance officials, including the current BOT governor, for the baht's plunge last year. \par \par \uc2  * In the Philippines, pre-election jitters undermined the peso despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate hikes to stem speculative pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the May 11 poll. \par \par \uc2  The central raised its overnight borrowing and lending rates by 50 basis points each. \par \par \uc2  * The peso languished below the 40.00 per dollar level, but traders said its falls would be limited by banks' dollar sales. \par \par \uc2  * In north Asia, the Hong Kong dollar was higher and forwards remained firm amid tight interbank liquidity and talk of overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4u06b3p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
