\par\par \b \uc2  ASIAN EXOTICS - Rupiah, baht easier in early trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 618 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  0120 GMT - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were little changed in early trade as dealers waded through a series of comments by regional \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials, but found little to surprise them. \par \par \uc2  * The Indonesian rupiah remained below the 8,000 per dollar level after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sjahril Sabirin said interest rates would stay high for the time being to support the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  * Sabirin said Bank Indonesia wanted to see the rupiah exchange rate go below 6,000 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  * Dealers said the forward market was already pricing in the prospect of higher interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "But the spot (dollar/rupiah) rate looks like it's not going above 8,200. It came off very fast from that level yesterday. I think the market is holding long dollar positions so we could see it lower," a U.S. bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  * A senior IMF official said the fund would make its next payments to Indonesia in three installments and added that the fund had misjudged the crisis in its early stage. \par \par \uc2  Bijan Aghelvi, deputy head of the IMF's Asia-Pacific region, said a proposed $3 billion payment from a $10 billion IMF loan to Indonesia would not be handed out at one time, but he declined to say exactly what Jakarta would get. \par \par \uc2  * The Thai baht was slightly weaker as the market turned apprehensive about its recent rally amid signs the government might not want it to strengthen further. \par \par \uc2  * Deputy Prime Minister Supachai Panitchpakdi said overnight he was happy with an exchange rate of 40 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  * "I don't see the baht continuing to strengthen from here once the buying euphoria is over. But we could see continuous (dollar) sell offers if there is more investment in Thai companies," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  * In the Philippines, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its overnight borrowing and lending rates by 50 basis points each, a move that was widely expected after it offered one-day reverse repos at 13.5 percent on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  * The bank wants to stem speculative pressure on the peso ahead of the May 11 presidential election, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to gain much support from the move, remaining below 40.00 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  * Elsewhere, the ringgit was stronger despite Kuala Lumpur's apparent rejection of an IMF call for higher Malaysian interest rates in its recent annual review of the economy. \par \par \uc2  * Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad on Wednesday defended Malaysia's stance of keeping interest rates at current levels. \par \par \uc2  "We have already tightened so much that businesses are screaming because they can't breathe. How much tighter do they want it to be," Mahathir was quoted as saying by the national Bernama news agency. \par \par \uc2  * Some dealers attributed the ringgit's rise to rumours Singapore had agreed to buy land owned by Malaysia's state railway firm on the island for 30 billion ringgit. \par \par \uc2  * In north Asia, the Hong Kong dollar was firm and forwards extended their late Wednesday gains amid some talk of overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA). \par \par \uc2  * But the HKMA said the outflow from the banking system on Wednesday was due to a commercial order and not related to speculative activities. \par \par \uc2  * HKMA chief Joseph Yam said discipline was the key to maintaining stability of the Hong Kong dollar's peg to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  * The South Korean won made a firm start amid abundant dollar liquidity, but dealers said further gains would be slowed by growing caution due to the weakening yen and signs the government did not want to see a steep drop in the dollar. \par \par \uc2  * The Taiwan dollar was steady while the Singapore dollar was slightly firmer. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4u06avu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
