\par\par \b \uc2  Equities Insight:HK Shrs Seen Opening Up; U.S. Rates Eyed \b0\par\par\uc2 356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 1998\par 03:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones Asian Equities Report \par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong stocks may open higher Thursday on the back of a gain on Wall Street overnight but the main index will likely quickly reverse direction amid ongoing concern about a possible interest rate increase in the U.S., according to analysts. \par \par \uc2  The blue chip Hang Seng Index closed Wednesday at 10,471.15, down 207.46 points. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones Industrial Average gained 52.56 points to close at 8951.52 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Even though the U.S. isn't expected to raise rates at the next meeting of the U.S. Federal Reserve's rate-setting Federal Open Market Committee in May, talk of a rate increase is fuelling concern in the local market, said George Chan, an analyst at Cheerful Securities. \par \par \uc2  The talk is aimed at slowing the U.S. economy because a rate increase in the U.S. would affect Asian economies and equity markets, which isn't what the U.S. wants right now, he said. \par \par \uc2  In the meantime, though, talk alone will likely hit Asian equities markets including Hong Kong, he said. \par \par \uc2  Ben Kwong, an analyst at Dharmala Securities, said a lack of any positive local news will also push Hong Kong's benchmark Hang Seng index toward 10,000 points in the coming sessions. \par \par \uc2  'Market sentiment remains very cautious. The index may test the lower levels in the absence of any positive news,' he said. On Thursday, the index will likely test the initial support level of 10,300 points, Kwong predicted. \par \par \uc2  A sharp climb of Hong Kong interbank rates Wednesday and talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stablilze the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't expected to affect the equity market Thursday, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  But if the rates continue to climb, the rise will certainly provide further pressure on the market, they said. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rates was sharply higher at 6.5% Wednesday, compared with 4.25% late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  By Kirsti Hastings; 852 2802-7002; Khastings@AP.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  30-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0142GMT \par \par \uc2  5013 55108 \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020010914du4u00gmh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
