\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Weaker Late On US$ Buying; Support Seen At HK$7.75 \b0\par\par\uc2 339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 1998\par 11:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is trading in a narrow range close to the key support level of HK$7.7500 per U.S. dollar late Monday, despite considerable buying of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by overseas entities. \par \par \uc2  At 0905 GMT (5:05 a.m. EDT), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7499-7.7500 per U.S. dollar, marginally weaker than the HK$7.7495 rate late Friday and early Monday. \par \par \uc2  'Market players and customers are keen on buying the U.S. dollar against the Hong Kong dollar,' said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  The buying from overseas has bid up the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has so far prevented the exchange rate from rising above the official support level of HK$7.7500. The HKMA is believed to have standing U.S. dollar sell orders lodged with a number of large banks at that level to cool the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said Hongkong & Shanghai Banking Corp. was seen buying Hong Kong dollars in the market when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit HK$7.7500 against the U.S. dollar. He said the bank might be purchasing the Hong Kong dollar on behalf of the HKMA. \par \par \uc2  In the forward exchange market, forward premiums rose slightly late Monday, with market players displaying a keener interest in holding the U.S. dollar longer term. \par \par \uc2  The three-month premium is at 190 points to the spot rate, up from 100 points late Friday and early Monday. The six-month premium is up at 630 points from Friday's 520 points. The one-month contract is at a 10-point premium to the spot rate, compared with a 15-point discount late Friday. \par \par \uc2  -By Daisy S.Y. Wong; 852-2802-7002; dwong@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 27-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0915GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4r03hgl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
