\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Steady Early, Hovers Close To Key Support Level \b0\par\par\uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 April 1998\par 05:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is steady early Friday, but is just a hair's breadth from a key support level after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Around 0240 GMT (10:40 p.m. EST), the Hong Kong dollar is quoted at HK$7.7498 against the U.S. dollar, unchanged from late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar has traded in a range of HK$7.7495 and HK$7.7498 so far Friday. \par \par \uc2  That's approaching HK$7.7500, which is seen as an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'That's very close - very, very close. It makes you wonder who's up there at HK$7.7498/99,' said a dealer with a local bank. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar was traded at HK$7.7500 late Thursday in Hong Kong and the HKMA was seen selling U.S. dollars for Hong Kong dollars at HK$7.7500 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with an Australasian institution said there was buying interest in London at HK$7.7500 overnight. \par \par \uc2  While standing HKMA sell orders at HK$7.7500 make it unlikely that the spot Hong Kong dollar will be pushed through that level, forwards are edging back up, reversing the trend of the past few days. \par \par \uc2  The local dealer said she heard some U.S. investment banks were buying forwards overnight in New York, although dealers downplayed the prospect of a speculative attack. \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the one-month premium was quoted at minus 18 points, from 30 points early Thursday. The three-month premium was quoted at 95 points, up from 85 points. The six-month premium was quoted at 490 points, up from 470 points. The one-year premium was quoted at 1600, up from 1550 points. \par \par \uc2  The volatile overnight Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rates is quoted at 4.125%, compared with 4.00% late during the previous session. The three-month rate is 6.00%, unchanged from late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  For more Hibor news, please refer to Dow Jones page \par \par \uc2  -By Sean Kennedy; (852) 2802 7002; skennedy@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 24-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0314GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4o03fye\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
