\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Steady Midday As Hibor Holds At Low Levels \b0\par\par\uc2 312 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 1998\par 07:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--With interbank interest rates holding at low levels, there are few takers for the Hong Kong dollar, which is essentially flat Thursday from late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trading at HK$7.7495 per U.S. dollar at 0455 GMT (12:55 a.m. EDT), nearly steady from HK$7.7493 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The head of treasurys at a domestic bank said investors have traded only small amounts of Hong Kong and U.S. dollars through midday Thursday, with low local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest rates and the specter of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar bottled tightly between HK$7.7490 and HK$7.7499. \par \par \uc2  The treasury chief attributed the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's flat trading to French banks, which he declined to name, and a large overseas investment fund house, which were seen buying U.S. dollars. \par \par \uc2  Because the Hong Kong dollar hasn't broken over the HK$7.7500 per U.S. dollar in recent weeks, dealers might again try to move the HK dollar to as strong levels as possible. \par \par \uc2  That's unlikely Thursday, though, he said, noting that there is little reason to be heavy in the Hong Kong dollar when local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  interbank rates are at only 4.0%-8.0%. The low rates could put pressure on banks to cut lending and deposit rates Friday. \par \par \uc2  In the forward market, the one-month contract is trading at a discount of 30 points, compared with 23 points late Wednesday. The three-month forward premium is 80 points, down from 85, indicating an unwinding of positions. The six-month contract is at a 470-point premium to the spot exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  -By Adam S. Najberg; (852)2802-7002; naj@asiaonline.net \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 23-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0531GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4n03epc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
