\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Flat Late On Reports Of HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  At HK$7.75 \b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 1998\par 12:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar weakened briefly to HK$7.7500 late Thursday before reported quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  brought it back to levels nearly flat from the previous session, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0945 GMT (5:45 a.m. EDT), the Hong Kong dollar was quoted at HK$7.7495 against the U.S. dollar, nearly steady from HK$7.7493 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The key news Thursday afternoon was that the Hong Kong dollar touched HK$7.7500, and some market participants said the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen buying small amounts of Hong Kong dollars at that level to cool the U.S. dollar either directly, or through banks or money brokers. \par \par \uc2  An HKMA spokesman didn't immediately reply to phone calls seeking comment, but the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't typically comment on its daily market activities. \par \par \uc2  Some market participants reported small trades being done at HK$7.7500 to the U.S. dollar, a long-standing level of resistance that is expected to prompt \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the HKMA, the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The HKMA is believed to have standing U.S. dollar sell orders lodged at HK$7.7500. \par \par \uc2  One trader reported seeing the HKMA buying Hong Kong dollars at HK$7.7500, but discounted the significance of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to light trading volume. He said there's no sign that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation is picking up. \par \par \uc2  'It doesn't mean anything,' the trader said. 'There's no speculative activity (in the Hong Kong dollar), it's just a matter of supply and demand.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 23-04-98 \par \par \uc2  1004GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4n03e2s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
