\par\par \b \uc2  US/HK forwards end softer on HKMA's money offer. \b0\par\par\uc2 471 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, April 17 (Reuters) - Hong Kong dollar interbank rates ended moderately lower mainly on money offers by the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  in late trade, dealers said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  They said they heard the HKMA directly contacted individual banks to offer short-term money, mostly in the one-month tenor. Some sources said the Land Fund was also spotted in the money market. \par \par \uc2  The one-month was lower at 5.18-5.37 versus 5.43-5.5 at the open and at Thursday's close. The overnight rate was soft at 4.00-4.25 percent versus 4.06-4.125 at the open and 4.18-4.25 at the close. \par \par \uc2  The three-month was easier at 6.12-6.18 versus 6.18-6.25 at the open and 6.25-6.31 at the close. The six-month dipped to 7.06-7.25 from 7.12-7.25 at the open and 7.25-7.31 at the close. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they believed the HKMA would opt to keep rates soft to promote the development of fixed rate bonds and fixed rate mortgages. \par \par \uc2  Forwards dropped in tandem with local interbank rates, as some interest rate-swappers rushed to take profits. \par \par \uc2  The three-month forward dipped to a 3 1/2-week low at 90-100 points versus 125-145 at the open and 135-155 at the close. The six-month ended at 500-550 points, a three-week low, versus 570-620 at the open and 590-620 at the close. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar was steady at HK$7.7470/80 per U.S. dollar versus HK$7.7475/85 at the open and HK$7.7480/90 at the close. \par \par \uc2  However dealers maintained the underlying tone for the Hong Kong dollar remained weak on the soft yen. \par \par \uc2  "The yen would only have a moderate upward pressure on the Hong Kong interbank rates if it dips below 135, but if it weakens below 140 or 150, that could trigger another major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  attack," a dealer at a major U.S. bank said. \par \par \uc2  But traders said that as local money market sentiment has improved and local institutional players have become more sophisticated, it is more difficult - though not impossible - for speculators to move the market against the Hong Kong dollar in favour of their positions. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar kept its strength against the yen in late \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade on fading fears of joint G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen. The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was softer at 131.71 in late Hong Kong trade versus 131.33/38 at Tokyo's open but flat versus 131.70/80 at New York close. \par \par \uc2  - Angi Li Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2847 4039. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4h075x7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
