\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Flat Late; Investors Await Signs From G-7, Japan \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 1998\par 11:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is flat late Wednesday after bouncing around in a narrow range for most of the afternoon in the territory. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar is trading at a steady HK$7.7496 per U.S. dollar at 0930 GMT (5:30 a.m. EDT) from late Tuesday and isn't expected to make any radical moves in either direction, said the head of money markets at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  The money markets chief said investors are feeling confident about the Hong Kong dollar as markets in Japan and around the rest of Asia have quieted. \par \par \uc2  Some banks tried to move the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to HK$7.7500, especially late in Hong Kong trading, but found no takers at the level at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  or money markets to cool the U.S. dollar. The money markets chief said spot \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors are awaiting directional cues from the Group of Seven finance ministers' meeting later Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Investors could grow jittery if the Bank of Japan abruptly abandons its aggressive defense of the yen after the G-7 meeting, the money markets chief said. If the dollar climbs to Y135-136 from current levels under Y130, the Hong Kong dollar might weaken, the money markets chief said. \par \par \uc2  'We'll have to wait and see if the yen stays around this level,' the money markets chief said. \par \par \uc2  Still, she said she believes the Hong Kong dollar should hold firm, with investors less prone to sell on bouts of nerves after last year's regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis. \par \par \uc2  In the quiet forward markets, the one-month contract is at parity with the spot rate, the three-month premium is 150 points, compared with 160 points late Tuesday. The six-month premium is up a touch to 610 points from 600 points. \par \par \uc2  -By Adam S. Najberg; (852)2802-7002; naj@asiaonline.net \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 15-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0949GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4f034z9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
