\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Weakens In Thin Trading After 4-Day Holiday \b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 1998\par 07:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar weakened Tuesday morning in sluggish activity as forward premiums fell after a four-day trading layoff. \par \par \uc2  Around 0445 GMT (12:45 a.m. EDT), the Hong Kong dollar was quoted at HK$7.7496 per U.S. dollar by Dao Heng Bank, weaker than the HK$7.7490 level quoted late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said trading was quiet in general and there were no signs of any speculative pressure. \par \par \uc2  A stronger-than-expected opening level for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  triggered a spate of U.S. dollar buying when the market opened and pushed the Hong Kong dollar down. \par \par \uc2  'Maybe the opening level was too strong for the Hong Kong dollar. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened at around HK$7.7488-90. It was quickly sold down to HK$7.7493, then to HK$7.7496,' said a dealer at Dao Heng Bank. \par \par \uc2  After that flurry of activity, trading turned quiet, and the Hong Kong dollar stayed at that level for the rest of Tuesday morning. \par \par \uc2  One bank posted an 'ask' quote at the psychological support level of HK$7.750, but there were no takers, with participants wary of causing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cool the dollar if it topped that level. \par \par \uc2  The HKMA tends to step into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at HK$7.7500 or above. \par \par \uc2  Other dealers said the Hong Kong dollar's weakening was a natural reaction to lower forward premiums, which have been on a downward trend since last week. \par \par \uc2  In the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the one-month premium is quoted at five points from 15 points late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The three-month and six-month premiums are quoted at 160 points and 650 points respectively, unchanged from the last session. \par \par \uc2  For more Hibor news, please refer to Dow Jones, page \par \par \uc2  -By Noel Fung; (852)2802-7002; noel.fung@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 14-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0502GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4e032zi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
