\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Stronger Midday After 3-Day Layoff,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 1998\par 07:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is a touch stronger Tuesday in light activity after a three-day layoff. \par \par \uc2  The local dollar is trading at HK$7.7488 per U.S. dollar at 0502 GMT (1:02 a.m. EDT), stronger than the HK$7.7495 quoted late Friday before suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The HKMA was believed to have sold U.S. dollars at HK$7.7495 to prevent a run above HK$7.7500, which is seen as a key defense level by market participants, though the HKMA has never confirmed the level. Dealers said the HKMA moved to stabilize the Hong Kong dollar as the yen plummeted against the U.S. dollar ahead of a long holiday weekend in the territory. \par \par \uc2  Some participants were toying with the HK$7.7500 level on Friday, hoping to move the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  during a time when the HKMA's powers to counter speculation would be limited to its New York representative office. \par \par \uc2  Markets were closed Monday for the annual grave-sweeping holiday. \par \par \uc2  The head of money markets in a U.S. bank's treasury said she saw light two-way activity and no sign of HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday morning. She attributed the market calm to a drop in the overnight interbank offered rate and a slight strengthening by the yen on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  'The pressure is off' the Hong Kong dollar, she said, noting that many key players are sitting on the sidelines or their key dealers are on vacation due to an upcoming four-day weekend for the Easter holiday. \par \par \uc2  The forward markets are also quiet after a burst of panic-covering of short positions last Friday. The one-month premium is 45 points, down from 110 points, the three-month is down to 250 from 380 points and the six-month is down to 740 points from 1050 points. \par \par \uc2  -By Adam S. Najberg; (852)2802-7002; naj@asiaonline.net \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 07-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0510GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4702xq6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
