\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dollar Up Late; All Calm After Suspected  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 1998\par 11:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--Investors reacted calmly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday, moving the local dollar to slightly stronger levels in a quiet session. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar is trading at HK$7.7490 per U.S. dollar at 0900 GMT (5:00 a.m. EDT), slightly stronger than the HK$7.7495 figure recorded late Friday, just prior to suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came ahead of a three-day weekend, as dealers attempted to move the Hong Kong dollar to HK$7.7500, which is believed to be a key level of support for the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  That moved the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  briefly to HK$7.7460 before traders in London bought the U.S. dollar, moving the Hong Kong dollar back to a relatively weak HK$7.7495. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar traded at HK$7.7485 early Tuesday and has moved only mildly weaker on light commercial U.S. dollar buying. A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a European bank said there's not much interest in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , both because of a change in external circumstances and because of an upcoming four-day holiday at the end of this week. \par \par \uc2  'On Friday, the market was before a holiday, and other factors were not that good. The dollar-yen was moving higher, the Hong Kong stock market was moving down, interest rates were higher, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were higher,' she said. \par \par \uc2  But on Tuesday, the yen has strengthened slightly, the stock market stood virtually still and interbank rates have been falling. Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are mostly steady, leaving the Hong Kong dollar flat as well, she noted. \par \par \uc2  The forward markets remain listless as well. The one-month premium is 30 points, compared with 110 points late Friday. The three-month premium is 210 points from 380 points and the six-month is 750 points from 1050 points. \par \par \uc2  -By Adam S. Najberg; (852)2802-7002; naj@asiaonline.net \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 07-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0913GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4702xim\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
