\par\par \b \uc2  HK Dlr Early Quoted at HK$7.7510, But Not Traded \b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 1998\par 06:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar Friday flirted with a key support level at HK$7.75, but dealers have mixed views on the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  attack. \par \par \uc2  At 0315 GMT (10:15 p.m. EST), the Hong Kong dollar was quoted at HK$7.7510 against the U.S. dollar, but dealers said no trades have gone through at this level. The HK$7.75 level is seen as a trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Authority hasn't shown its hand yet. \par \par \uc2  At 0326 GMT (10:26 p.m. EST), the Hong Kong unit was quoted at a mid-rate of HK$7.7505 by AIG International, HK$7.7497 by HSBC Markets, and HK$7.7503 by First Pacific Bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said some banks are worried that speculators could mount a sustained attack on the Hong Kong dollar in New York and London where it's easier to move the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the more liquid Hong Kong market closes later Friday. They could renew the assault Monday, when there's a public holiday in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  'It's not a panic like last time,' said a local bank dealer, referring to an earlier assault on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January when the one-month forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate hit 950 points, and the one-year forward hit 7800 points. \par \par \uc2  Early Friday, the one-month was quoted at 45 points early Friday and the one-year at 2300. \par \par \uc2  The local bank dealer said he expects the Hong Kong dollar to be sold off after its local close later Friday. \par \par \uc2  An analyst with a U.S. institution said she's been told that some U.S. banks have already sold the Hong Kong dollar, but it's not a full-blown attack. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 03-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0405GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4302vuh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
