\par\par \b \uc2  HK Govt Official/ \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -2: Says Traders Know Better \b0\par\par\uc2 203 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 1998\par 11:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--A \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  government official denied the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets Friday to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Secretary for Financial Services Rafael Hui said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market participants are intuitive enough to know not to push the Hong Kong dollar below a key level without the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  having to do anything. \par \par \uc2  'At that level, each of the banks will know what happens and will build up Hong Kong dollar positions,' Hui told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Two traders said earlier Friday that they believed they saw the HKMA selling U.S. dollars at HK$7.7495 at 0730 GMT and a third said money brokers told him the HKMA sold dollars at 0645 GMT at the HK$7.7495 level and again at HK$7.7485 some 45 minutes later. \par \par \uc2  After flirting with HK$7.7500 for most of the day, the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened suddenly in afternoon trading, moving briefly to HK$7.7460 per dollar. It is quoted at HK$7.7480 at 0933 GMT. \par \par \uc2  -By Daisy S.Y. Wong; (852)2802-7002; dwong@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 03-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0938GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4302udg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
