\par\par \b \uc2  HKMA Believed To Have Sold -3: Brokers Report  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 309 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 1998\par 11:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The level of suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is close to what the market believes is the HKMA's defense line of HK$7.750. The quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has never said that it wants the Hong Kong dollar to trade in a band, but market participants widely believe it steps into markets when the Hong Kong dollar weakens to HK$7.75 or strengthens to HK$7.72. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar had flirted with the HK$7.75 per US$1.00 level all day Friday before strengthening abruptly to HK$7.7475 at around 0730 GMT (2:30 p.m. EST) \par \par \uc2  'There were some large U.S. dollar selling positions from major banks. The market reckoned that HKMA was behind it,' said Wong Chi-yiu, deputy chief dealer at Bank of China group treasury center. \par \par \uc2  A third trader said brokers who executed several transactions told him that the HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market twice Friday, starting at 0645 GMT and then again at 0730 GMT. \par \par \uc2  He said U.S. dollar selling by the HKMA was done at HK$7.7495 and then again at HK$7.7485. The two rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar strengthen to HK$7.7460 per dollar. The dealer reckoned the move was an echo of the Bank of Japan's market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier Friday and said he wonders whether it was part of a region-wide concerted effort to halt local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' slides. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trading at HK$7.7482 at 0900 GMT. \par \par \uc2  An HKMA spokesman wouldn't confirm or deny participants' suspicions, noting the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  typically doesn't comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its dealing room. \par \par \uc2  -By Noel Fung; (852)2802-7002; noel.fung@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 03-04-98 \par \par \uc2  0927GMT \par \par \uc2  1053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4302uba\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
