\par\par \b \uc2  US/HK forwards extend sharp gains as yen weaker. \b0\par\par\uc2 587 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  USD/HKD 7.7494/04    OVERNIGHT 4.50-5.00 3MO HKD/USD  DEPO   160 \par \par \uc2  USD/IDR 8,425/8,575  3MO SWAP 320-370    2YR HKD/USD  SPREAD 252 \par \par \uc2  USD/  Y 134.83/4.88  6MO SWAP 870-970   10YR HKD/USD  SPREAD 268 \par \par \uc2  ------------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2      *US/HK forwards extended gains as yen weakened further after \par \par \uc2  breaking the key support of 134 per U.S. dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      *The Hong Kong dollar rebounded slightly after slipping to a \par \par \uc2  three-month low of HK$7.7498/01 per U.S. dollar, a hair away \par \par \uc2  from its key support of HK$7.75, a level that traders said \par \par \uc2  would trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  (HKMA). \par \par \uc2      *The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at HK$7.7494/04 at \par \par \uc2  midsession, steady from HK$7.7493/03 at the open and \par \par \uc2  HK$7.7490/00 at Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2      *Dealers said they heard more than one note-issuing bank on \par \par \uc2  the bid side of the Hong Kong dollar spot, believed to be acting \par \par \uc2  on behalf of the HKMA in a bid to cap the strength of the U.S. \par \par \uc2  dollar. \par \par \uc2  *The three-month marched higher to 330-370 points against \par \par \uc2  270-300 in early trade and 230-260 at Thursday's close. The \par \par \uc2  six-month was up at 920-970 versus 880-930 points in early trade \par \par \uc2  and 775-830 at the close. \par \par \uc2      *Views were mixed on near-term outlook on forward rates. \par \par \uc2      *Some dealers believed rates were likely to firm further as \par \par \uc2  Europe or New York started trading. Overseas traders tended to \par \par \uc2  have a more bearish view on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. \par \par \uc2      *"You often see forwards firm up in late Hong Kong trade, \par \par \uc2  because that is the time London starts trading," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2      *Other dealers believed increasing offers on dollar forwards \par \par \uc2  for profit-taking were likely to cap the upside. \par \par \uc2      *"Many players who had gone long in forwards a few weeks \par \par \uc2  ago, as forwards rates plunged to pre-Asian crisis level, are \par \par \uc2  looking for opportunity to cover their positions" a dealer said. \par \par \uc2      *Frederic Laine, head of interest rate and derivative \par \par \uc2  trading at Credit Lyonnais, said he believed forwards would be \par \par \uc2  range-bound and he did not see major selling on the Hong Kong \par \par \uc2  dollar spot. \par \par \uc2      *Local term money rates were moderately firmer across the \par \par \uc2  board partly on routine demand ahead of the long weekend and the \par \par \uc2  rising risk premium of the Hong Kong dollar on the fall in yen. \par \par \uc2      *Hong Kong financial markets will close on April 6 for a \par \par \uc2  public holiday and reopen from April 7 to 9 before closing again \par \par \uc2  on April 10 and 13 for the Easter holidays. \par \par \uc2      "Interbank liquidity was tighter than yesterday but still \par \par \uc2  abundant especially at the short end," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2      Overnight rates remained below five percent, quoted at \par \par \uc2  4.5-5.0 percent versus 4.43-4.93 in early trade and 4.68-4.75 at \par \par \uc2  Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2      The one-month was moderately firmer at 6.0-6.12 versus \par \par \uc2  5.87-6.0 in early trade and 5.46-5.60 at the close. \par \par \uc2      The three-month was steady at 7.25-7.37 versus 7.18-7.37 in \par \par \uc2  early trade but firmer than 6.75-7.00 at the close. The \par \par \uc2  six-month was unchanged at 7.75-8.12 against its open but firmer \par \par \uc2  than 7.50-7.75 at the close. \par \par \uc2  -Angi Li 852-2847-4039; Fax 852-2845-0636. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du43080u7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
