\par\par \b \uc2  ASIAN EXOTICS-Regionals lick wounds after yen blow. \b0\par\par\uc2 445 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  0420 GMT - Regionals limp at lower levels after the yen was stunned by Moody's negative Japan rating. \par \par \uc2  * Early gains on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are wiped out as dollar advances to six-year high of 134.85 against beleaguered yen. \par \par \uc2  * Moody's Investors Services changes outlook for Japan's country ceiling and domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating for the government to negative from stable. \par \par \uc2  * Dealers say dollar/yen movements continue to set direction for regionals, with the exception of Indonesia's rupiah. \par \par \uc2  * Rupiah avoids direct blows because of the talks between the government and International Monetary Fund (IMF), especially on restructing private debt. \par \par \uc2  * "The market is awaiting something surprising from the talks, particularly on how to solve the corporate foreign debt problem, as this would help ease corporate dollar demand," a bank dealer in Indonesia said. \par \par \uc2  * At 0430 GMT, spot rupiah is quoted at 8,475/675 at 0200 GMT compared with 8,525/625 late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  * The Thai baht tumbles to intraday lows at 41.20/40 per dollar versus late Thursday's 40.65/85 on yen woes and fear of higher interest rates. \par \par \uc2  * Raising of key lending rates by Thailand's top commercial banks is viewed negatively by the market. \par \par \uc2  * The ringgit falls to 3.7750/50 against the dollar in line with the spike in dollar/yen and corporate demand for dollars. \par \par \uc2  * It earlier trades to 3.7300, then descends sharply with support seen for near term around 3.8300. \par \par \uc2  * Dollar/Sing gains to 1.6330 before retreating to 1.6295/25 on profit taking, against late Thursday's 1.6280/90. \par \par \uc2  * North Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are pushed lower by yen's declines on the dollar. \par \par \uc2  * "Dollar/won has jumped up quite a bit even on the forwards," says a dealer with an Asian institution. \par \par \uc2  * The South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to slide on dollar demand for interest payments on foreign debt due next week. \par \par \uc2  * Won is quoted at 1,451/61 at midday compared with 1,438/46 early and a close of 1,413 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  * The Taiwan dollar comes off lows to stand at T$32.939/959 versus Thursday's close of T$32.887. \par \par \uc2  * It gets a lift from Taiwan deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Hsu Chia-tung saying there is no need to let Taiwan's dollar depreciate to stimulate sagging exports. \par \par \uc2  * Dealers say competitive export issues have been dampening sentiment on Taiwan dollar and Korean won this week. \par \par \uc2  * The Hong Kong dollar stabilises at HK$7.7492/02 after flirting with HK$7.75 level, which dealers speculate would trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du43080so\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (hong kong near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or t